  'grogach', 'Grogach', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but typically Unprincipled (15%), Anarchist (50%), or Miscreant (25%)', '{"IQ":"2D6+2","ME":"2D6+4","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6+12","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+48', NULL, NULL, 'Spd is 3D6 running or 6D6 flying. In S.D.C.-rule settings: A.R. 10, 6D6 S.D.C., P.E. x3 for Hit Points. P.P.E. is not printed for this entry.', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":2,"strike":3,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"pull":3,"roll":5}', '+6 save vs Horror Factor; impervious to spoiled food and poison; +2 on all saving throws.; attacks per melee: Three physical or two using magic; pull: +3 (pull punch); roll: +5 (roll with impact/punch/fall); damage: As per Supernatural P.S.', 'Speaks Faerie and Gobblely 98%; PCs may learn 2 more languages at base+20%. Identify Plants & Fruit 75%, Brew 90%, Cook 80%, Preserve Food 80%, Recognize/Use Poison 70%, Carpentry 80%, Boat Building 60%, Land Navigation 90%, Wilderness Survival 90%, Track Animals 75%, Faerie Lore 90%, Climb 70%/60%, Horsemanship: General 80%, W.P. two of choice. Skills do not increase.', 'Flies/hovers even without wings up to 200 ft, Supernatural P.S. and P.E., nightvision 90 ft, sees invisible, senses crops/fruit trees (70%), fertile soil (45%), and ley lines (40%).', 'Earth Warlock magic: Dowsing, Dig, Animate Plants, Grow Plants, Wither Plants, Repel Animals, Travel Through Earth, Chameleon, and jinxing a weapon/tool', NULL, '3-4 feet tall (0.9-1.2 m)', '80-100 pounds (36-45 kg)', 'Around 5000 years or longer', 'Wanders wilderness and farmland; found in Coalition States of Missouri and Iowa; uncomfortable in cities/towns', 'farmers it helps; other Faerie Folk generally', NULL, NULL, 'Burly, brown-furred faerie farmhand who loves growing crops and cooking, but ruins farms and jinxes tools when angered.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.120-121');
  'hairy-jack', 'Hairy Jack', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but typically Anarchist (25%), Miscreant (30%), Diabolic (40%)', '{"IQ":"1D6+2","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6+10","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+60', NULL, NULL, 'Spd is 3D6 as a humanoid or 6D6 as a boar. In S.D.C.-rule settings: A.R. 10, 1D4x10+10 S.D.C., P.E. x3 for Hit Points. P.P.E. is not printed for this entry.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"pull":1,"roll":2}', '+6 save vs Horror Factor; +2 on all saving throws. Book''s own note: not recommended as a player character.; attacks per melee: Three physical or two using magic; pull: +1 (pull punch); roll: +2 (roll with impact/punch/fall); damage: As per Supernatural P.S.; claw +2D6 M.D., bite 2D6 M.D.', 'Speaks Faerie and Gobblely 98%, Recognize/Use Poison 60%, Land Navigation 90%, Wilderness Survival 90%, Track Animals 70%, Track Humanoids 60%, Faerie Lore 60%, Climb 70%/60%, Horsemanship: General 50%, W.P. three of choice. Skills do not increase. Not recommended as a player character.', 'Supernatural P.S., nightvision 200 ft, sees invisible, can turn invisible at will, prowl 45%, and can transform into a wild boar.', 'Repel Animals, Chameleon, Fear, Charm, and jinxing a weapon/tool', NULL, '4-5 feet tall (1.2-1.5 m)', '100-150 pounds (45-67.5 kg)', 'About two to three hundred years', 'Old barns, dead trees, swamps, bogs, caves, underground ruins, dilapidated places; found in the Kingdom of Tolkeen and the ''Burbs of Chi-Town, Iron Heart, Free Quebec', 'other mean/evil Faerie Folk; brigands; criminal gangs (works as enforcer)', NULL, NULL, 'Pig-headed, foul-tempered faerie thug that tortures captives and cattle, often working as muscle for gangs or brigands.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.121');
  'leprechaun', 'Leprechaun', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, mostly Anarchist (70%), Unprincipled (15%), Miscreant (15%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6+3","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"2D6+2","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6 min 8","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+50', '1D6x100', NULL, 'In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx6, S.D.C. 5D6, A.R. 8', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1,"roll":2}', '+3 to save vs magic, +2 to save vs Horror Factor. P.B. has a minimum of 8.', 'Speak Faerie and Dragonese 98%; PCs learn two more languages plus literacy in one at base+30% skill bonus. Land Navigation 55%, Wilderness Survival 60%, Preserve Food 60%, Recognize Precious Metals/Stones 96%, Track Animals 40%, Faerie Lore 90%, Sing 60%, Dance 70%, Swim 80%, Prowl 40%, Climb 60%/50%, Palming 60%, Concealment 60%, Pick Pockets 82%, Pick Locks 55%, Locksmith 40%, Basic Electronics 70%, Streetwise 54%, Operate Computer 55%, plus two W.P. of choice. Skills do not increase.', 'Nightvision 60 ft, keen normal vision, turns invisible at will, ventriloquism 88%, and automatically senses secret compartments or doors 64%.', 'Escape, Chameleon, Charismatic Aura, Detect Concealment, Concealment, Reduce Self to Six Inches, Fools Gold', NULL, 'Two to three feet tall (0.6-0.9 m)', '1D4x10+40 pounds', NULL, NULL, 'Faerie Folk', NULL, NULL, 'A dapper, three-foot fey trickster and hoarder of treasure, famous for con artistry, heavy drinking, and never betraying its own kind.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.122');
  'nymph', 'Nymph', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, usually Principled (40%) or Scrupulous (40%)', '{"IQ":"3D6+1","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"2D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"2D6+6","PB":"3D6+6 min 16","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+30', '1D6x100', NULL, 'Flying Spd is 2D6x10+40; ground Spd is 3D6. Impervious to S.D.C. and non-magic M.D. weapons.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx4, S.D.C. 6D6, A.R. 7', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":1,"strike":2}', '+3 to save vs Nature Magic (Spoiling, Shamanistic, etc.), +1 to save vs other magic and poison, +2 to save vs Horror Factor. P.B. has a minimum of 16.; damage: as per Supernatural P.S., or by spell', 'Magically speaks all languages 98%, Basic Math 98%, Identify Plants & Fruit 98%, Botany 98%, Biology 60%, Holistic Medicine 98%, Astronomy 98%, Land Navigation 98%, Wilderness Survival 98%, Preserve Food 98%, Cook 80%, Track Animals 90%, Faerie Lore 98%, Demon & Monster Lore 60%, Sing 60%, Dance 60%, Prowl 80%, Climb 90%/80%. Skills do not increase. Not recommended as a player character.', 'Flies, has supernatural strength, sees the invisible, turns invisible at will, senses water and ley lines, magically speaks all languages, resists all but magic and psionics, can merge into a living plant, and passes through wood, earth or stone.', 'Sleep, Dust Storm, Summon Fog, Purple Mist, Call Lightning, Wind Rush, Finger of the Wind, Thunder Clap, Extinguish Fires, Part Waters, Calm Waters, Calm Storms, Repel Animals, Grow Plants, Animate Plants, Wall of Thorns, Breath of Life, Ley Line Transmission, Faeries Dance', NULL, 'Six feet (1.8 m)', 'Three ounces (85 grams)', NULL, 'An adopted domain of 1D4x10+10 miles, centered on an ancient tree, boulder, river, well, spring, cave or hill; seen by day at beautiful spots with Faeries or Sprites', 'Faeries; Sprites; Pixies; Brownies', 'those who harm her land or its Faerie inhabitants', NULL, 'A gentle nature spirit bound to a natural landmark, appearing as a glowing elf-maiden who secretly protects her woodland domain from harm.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.122-123');
  'pixie-common', 'Pixie: Common', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, lean toward Anarchist (40%) and Unprincipled (40%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"1D6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6","PB":"3D6+1 min 9","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+25', '1D6x100', NULL, 'Flying Spd is 2D6x10+50; ground Spd is 4D6.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx6, S.D.C. 5D6, A.R. 8', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":2,"pull":2,"roll":2}', '+2 on all saving throws, +6 to save vs Horror Factor. P.B. has a minimum of 9.', 'Speak Faerie and Gobblely 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+20% skill bonus. Identify Plants & Fruit 60%, Land Navigation 62%, Wilderness Survival 70%, Preserve Food 60%, Track Animals 50%, Faerie Lore 90%, Sing 50%, Dance 64%, Gymnastics 64%, Pick Pockets 50%, Pick Locks 40%, Prowl 60%, Climb 70%/60%, plus three ancient W.P.s of choice. Skills do not increase.', 'Flies and hovers though wingless, nightvision 60 ft, keen normal vision, turns invisible at will, and senses ley lines 50%.', 'Charm, Sleep, Wind Rush, Globe of Daylight, Mend Wood & Clay, Tongues, Chameleon, Circle of Rain', NULL, '12 inches tall (0.3 m)', 'One pound (0.45 kg)', NULL, 'Fields, meadows, and small groves of trees', 'Faerie Folk', NULL, NULL, 'A twelve-inch wingless fey who can still fly, sturdier and less delicate than a Faerie, and just as fond of harmless mischief.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.123');
  'pixie-frost', 'Pixie: Frost', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, lean toward Anarchist (50%) and Unprincipled (40%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"1D6+1","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6","PB":"4D6 min 16","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+25', '1D6x100', NULL, 'Flying Spd is 2D6x10+100; ground Spd is 4D6.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx6, S.D.C. 5D6, A.R. 8', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"pull":2,"roll":2}', '+2 on all saving throws, +6 to save vs Horror Factor. P.B. has a minimum of 16.', 'Speak Faerie and Dragonese 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+20% skill bonus. Land Navigation 62%, Wilderness Survival 70%, Preserve Food 70%, Track Animals 50%, Faerie Lore 90%, Sing 50%, Dance 64%, Gymnastics 64%, Swim 60%, Prowl 50%, Climb 80%/70%, plus two ancient W.P.s of choice. Skills do not increase.', 'Immune to cold, nightvision 60 ft, keen normal vision, turns invisible at will, senses ley lines 30%, and passes through ice as if it were air.', 'Globe of Daylight, Wind Rush, North Wind, Freeze Water, Hail, Snow Storm, Wall of Ice, Frostblade', NULL, '12 inches tall (0.3 m)', 'One pound (0.45 kg)', NULL, 'Cold, cool or moderate climates: snow, ice, glaciers, mountaintops; Great Lakes, northern Canada, Scandinavia, Siberia', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A one-foot, blue-skinned frost fey immune to cold that freezes foes with icy breath or touch across northern snowy regions.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.123-124');
  'puck', 'Puck', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any selfish or evil, lean toward Miscreant (40%) and Diabolic (50%)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"2D6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"4D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+55', '1D6x100', NULL, 'In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx3, S.D.C. 1D4x10+10, A.R. 10', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', '+6 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 on all saving throws. GM may add 1D6+2 Russian Spoiling Magic spells.', 'Speaks Faerie and Gobblely 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+10% skill bonus. Land Navigation 70%, Wilderness Survival 75%, Track Animals 60%, Track Humans 55%, Faerie Lore 85%, Demon & Monster Lore 70%, Dance 75%, Prowl 50%, Palming 55%, Concealment 48%, Pick Pockets 60%, Pick Locks 65%, Streetwise 48%, Climb 90%/80%, Swim 80%, plus two Piloting skills and five W.P.s of choice. Skills do not increase.', 'Supernatural strength, nightvision 90 ft, senses water and ley lines 50%, and can shift into the shape of a pony, a wild boar, a goat or a dog.', 'Spoil, Repel Animals, Death Trance, Concealment', NULL, 'Three to four feet tall (0.9-1.2 m)', '3D6+60 pounds', NULL, 'Dark, solitary places of foul or evil appearance: caves, sewers, swamps, bogs, ruins', NULL, 'Big folk (humans); pretty Faerie Folk', NULL, 'A black-hearted, demonic-looking satyr-like fey that tortures victims and hoards loot from dark, foul lairs in small evil bands.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.124-125');
  'spriggan', 'Spriggan', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, lean toward Anarchist (50%) and Miscreant (30%)', '{"IQ":"2D6+1","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"6D6+20","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6+6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+45', '1D6x100', NULL, 'In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx4, S.D.C. 1D4x10+10, A.R. 10', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"strike":1,"parry":3,"roll":3,"pull":6}', '+6 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 on all saving throws.; damage: as per Supernatural P.S., or by magic or weapon', 'Speaks Faerie and Gobblely 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+10% skill bonus. Basic Math 92%, Art (sculpting/building) 75%, Carpentry 75%, Boat Building 75%, Basic Electronics 75%, Land Navigation 75%, Wilderness Survival 75%, Preserve Food 75%, Faerie Lore 90%, Dance 45%, Prowl 45%, Climb 60%/50%, Swim 75%, Pilot/Horsemanship 75%, plus two more Pilot skills, W.P. Blunt and three other W.P.s. Skills do not increase.', 'Supernatural strength and endurance, nightvision 40 ft, senses nearby Earth Elementals 65%, and passes through stone, rock or clay as if it were air.', 'Dust Storm, Hopping Stones, Mend Stone, Crumble Stone, Rock to Mud, Clay to Stone, Stone to Flesh', NULL, 'Two and a half to three feet tall (0.75-0.9 m)', '2D6+50 pounds', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'everybody, including other Faerie Folk', NULL, 'A husky, grumpy three-foot fey obsessed with raising stone monoliths and crop circles, and hostile toward nearly everyone.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.125');
  'sprite-tree', 'Sprite: Tree', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, lean toward Anarchist (60%)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"1D6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6+1","PB":"3D6+7 min 16","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+8', '1D6x100', NULL, 'Flying Spd is 3D6x10+60; ground Spd is 3D6.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx2, S.D.C. 3D6, A.R. 6', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":3,"strike":1,"dodge":4}', '+2 on all saving throws. Dodge in flight is automatic and does not use an attack. P.B. has a minimum of 16.', 'Speak Faerie 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+10% skill bonus. Identify Plants & Fruit 98%, Land Navigation 90%, Wilderness Survival 90%, Preserve Food 90%, Faerie Lore 90%, Sing 80%, Dance 84%, Prowl 80%, Climb 80%/70%, Acrobatics 80%. Skills do not increase.', 'Flies and hovers, nightvision 90 ft, sees the invisible, keen normal vision, and senses water and ley lines.', 'Chameleon, Charm, Animate Plants, Faeries Dance', NULL, '4 inches tall (101 mm)', 'Three ounces (85 grams)', NULL, 'Tree canopies; seen at dawn and dusk; travels in groups of 8-48', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A cheerful, four-inch yellow-green tree-dwelling fey that raids beehives and nectar and pranks travelers at dawn and dusk.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.125-126');
  'sprite-water', 'Sprite: Water', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, lean toward Anarchist (60%)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"1D6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6+2","PB":"3D6+7 min 16","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+10', '1D6x100', NULL, 'Flying Spd is 3D6x10+40; ground Spd is 4D6.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx2, S.D.C. 3D6, A.R. 6', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"dodge":4}', '+1 to save vs magic and poison. Dodge in flight is automatic like a parry. P.B. has a minimum of 16.', 'Speak Faerie 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+10% skill bonus. Identify Plants & Fruit 60%, Land Navigation 85%, Wilderness Survival 85%, Preserve Food 85%, Faerie Lore 80%, Sing 60%, Dance 70%, Prowl 60%, Climb 50%/40%, Swim 98%, Horsemanship: Frogs 70%. Skills do not increase.', 'Flies and hovers, nightvision 90 ft (sees in total darkness), sees the invisible, holds its breath 4D4 minutes, and senses water and ley lines.', 'Befuddle, Swim as the Fish, Summon Fog, Summon & Control Animals (frogs only), Circle of Rain, Purple Fog', NULL, '4 inches tall (101 mm)', 'Three ounces (85 grams)', NULL, 'Glens, meadows, quiet pools and gentle streams; seen at dawn and dusk near water; travels in groups of 6-36', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A pale, dark-haired water fey with blue wings that teases frogs, fishermen and travelers near ponds and streams.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.126');
  'sprite-wind-puffs', 'Sprite: Wind-Puffs', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Lean toward Anarchist and Unprincipled', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"1D6","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"2D6","PB":"3D6+8 min 16","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+6', '1D6x100', NULL, 'Flying Spd is 3D6x10+40; ground Spd is 4D6.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx2, S.D.C. 3D6, A.R. 6', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":3,"dodge":4}', '+1 to save vs magic and psionics. Dodge in flight is automatic like a parry. P.B. has a minimum of 16.', 'R.C.C.: Creature of magic and nature/Faerie wilderness scout. Speak Faerie 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+10% skill bonus. Identify Plants & Fruit 75%, Land Navigation 75%, Wilderness Survival 75%, Preserve Food 75%, Faerie Lore 75%, Sing 75%, Dance 75%, Prowl 60%, Climb 50%/40%, Swim 50%, Horsemanship: Exotic Animal: Butterflies 60%. Skills do not increase.', 'Flies and hovers, nightvision 90 ft, sees the invisible, keen normal vision, and senses water and ley lines.', 'Charm, Mend Wood & Clay, Globe of Daylight, Fingers of the Wind, Wind Rush, Faeries Dance', NULL, '4 inches tall (101 mm)', 'Three ounces (85 grams)', NULL, 'Fields of flowers and grassy plains; travels in groups of 6-36', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A shy, curious flower-field fey with puff-like wings that rummages through sleeping travelers belongings and ties knots in laces.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.126');
  'toad-stools', 'Toad Stools', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, lean toward Miscreant (40%), Diabolic (40%) and Anarchist (15%)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"1D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+46', '1D6x100', NULL, 'In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx3, S.D.C. 1D4x10+10, A.R. 10', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', '+6 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 on all saving throws.', 'Speaks Faerie and Gobblely 98%; PCs learn two more languages at base+10% skill bonus. Identify Plants & Fruit 55%, Land Navigation 60%, Wilderness Survival 80%, Track Animals/Faeries 55%, Faerie Lore 85%, Sing 45%, Dance 55%, Climb 70%/60%, Swim 98%. Skills do not increase.', 'Nightvision 90 ft (total darkness), holds breath up to 30 minutes, senses water and ley lines, and can transform into an ordinary toad. Touching one with bare skin curses the toucher with 1D6 painful warts that lower P.B., initiative and skill performance until removed by Remove Curse.', 'Summon Fog, Animate Plants, Spoil (water only), Repel Animals', NULL, 'Two to three feet long (0.6-0.9 m)', '2D6+40 pounds', NULL, 'Swamps, bogs, and humid caves and caverns, among mushrooms', 'Bogies; Pucks; other evil Faerie Folk', 'smaller, prettier Faerie Folk (Sprites, Faeries, Pixies)', NULL, 'An ugly, wart-covered toad-like fey bandit that lurks in swamps, bites with poison, and curses anyone who touches its skin.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.126-127');
  'will-o-the-wisp', 'Will-O-The-Wisp', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but tend toward good or selfish', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"4D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"2D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"1D6"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+400', NULL, 'MEx3', 'M.D.C. figure is for the main body; individual branches carry 2D6 to 6D6 M.D. depending on size.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx8, S.D.C. 2D4x100, A.R. 10', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":6}', '+3 on all saving throws, +6 to save vs Horror Factor.', 'Communicates telepathically, plus Identify Plants & Fruit 95%, Dowsing 90%, Astronomy 80%, Faerie Lore 95%, Lore: Demons & Monsters 70%, Lore: Geomancy 60%. Skills do not increase.', 'Sees 300 feet in all directions day or night, senses fire within a mile, and animates/controls its host tree, using branches as hands and limbs.', 'Circle of Rain, Call Lightning, Extinguish Fires, Mend Cloth, Globe of Daylight, Earth Rumble, Wind Rush, Create Fog, Purple Mist (usual Faerie Magic limitations apply)', 'Presence Sense, Object Read, Sense Magic, Sense Evil, Commune with Animals, Telepathy', 'Varies, depending on the size of the tree it inhabits', NULL, NULL, 'Bonded to a single large, old tree; rare, but known in eastern Canada, the Magic Zone, the British Isles, France and Germany', 'Faerie Folk (may guard the treasure of a Faerie friend)', 'those who desecrate its tree or harm nearby Faerie Folk or fauna', NULL, 'A spirit permanently bound to an old tree, invisible until linked, that can animate its branches to fight in defense of its territory.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.127-128');
  'angel-demon-serpent', 'Angel-Demon Serpent', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Split personality: good side Unprincipled (leaning Aberrant), evil side Miscreant (leaning Unprincipled)', '{"IQ":"2D6+4","ME":"1D6","MA":"2D6+4","PS":"2D6+18","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"2D6+5","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D4x10+PE', 'PEx10', 'ME+4D6', 'S.D.C.-world stats given for use off Rifts Earth. M.D.C. gains +12 per level of experience; Hit Points (S.D.C. worlds) gain +10 per level; P.P.E. gains +10 per level; I.S.P. gains +1D6 per level. Spd is 3D6+6 running/slithering or 4D6+44 (35-45 mph) flying. P.S. and P.E. are Supernatural.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 6D6+30, S.D.C. 1D4x10+16, A.R. 10', NULL, 11, '{"initiative":2,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":3}', '+6 to save vs Horror Factor, +6 to save vs possession (impervious to possession by supernatural beings); punches and magic do double damage to supernatural evil beings; demon blades made to slay angels do double damage to it; silver has no special effect.; attacks per melee: Those gained from Hand to Hand: Martial Arts and level of experience, plus two additional attacks/actions per melee; initiative: +2 on the ground, +4 from the air; dodge: +3 on the ground, +5 airborne', 'Lore: Demons and Monsters +25%, Basic Math +10%, Land Navigation +20%, Astronomy +10%, Navigation +10%, Tracking Humanoids +10% (+15% vs demons/Deevils/humanoid monsters), Track Animals +10%, Identify Plants and Fruits +15%, Climb, Swim, W.P. Blunt, Hand to Hand: Martial Arts, plus two Military skills of choice +10% (excludes Field Armorer)', 'Flies 35-45 mph, hawk vision, nightvision 2000 ft, sees invisible, immune to cold, poison, disease, and possession, resists heat, swims to 1 mile deep, prehensile tail strike, bio-regenerates 2D6 per round, regrows limbs in 48 hours, needs little sleep.', 'Knows all Water and Fire Warlock spells levels 1-5, plus any cold/ice Warlock spells, Eternal Flame, Flame of Life, and Fire Whip; P.P.E. 200+', 'Minor Psychic: Meditation, Mind Block, Empathy', '14-18 feet long (4.3-5.5 m); stands 7-8 feet (2.1-2.4 m) at the shoulder, can raise or lower to match a companion 3-12 ft tall', '800-1,000 lbs (360-450 kg)', 'Appears immortal but only remembers its last 500-1000 years; can be slain by magic, psionics or violence', 'Palladium World: Northern Hinterlands, Ophid''s Grasslands, Great Northern Mountains, believed under 10,000 total. Rifts Earth: Calgary and Detroit-Windsor Rifts, Magic Zone, US-Mexico border, Yucatan, Africa, France, Russia, China, always in small numbers', 'Potentially anybody, but prefers Men at Arms and practitioners of magic', 'True demons and Deevils; Elementals; gods; the undead; Witches; Necromancers; most dark beings of Atlantis, Calgary Monster Kingdom, China', 'Not available as a standard O.C.C. path; functions as a Soldier-Warlock dual-class R.C.C.', 'A dual-natured, serpent-bodied winged Elf-like being embodying conflicting angelic and demonic personalities, tied to fire and water magic.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.130-133');
  'beast-dragon', 'Beast Dragon', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but almost always Diabolic (50%), Miscreant (40%), or Aberrant (5%)', '{"IQ":"1D6+3","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6+10","PP":"3D6+6","PE":"5D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6x10', '1D6x10', NULL, 'Three heads with separate brains: I.Q. is 1D6+3 for the lion head, 1D6+1 for the antelope head, 1D6 for the serpent head (all work as one). M.D.C. figures are for the main body on Rifts Earth; each of the three heads separately has 1D4x10+20 M.D.C., and destroying all three heads slays the creature. S.D.C.-world stats: Hit Points 6D6x10, S.D.C. 3D6x10 (main body) plus 1D4x10 per head, Natural A.R. 12.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 6D6x10, S.D.C. 3D6x10, A.R. 12', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":9,"initiative":4,"strike":3,"parry":4,"dodge":6}', '+3 on all saving throws, in addition to attribute bonuses. Typical treasure trove: 4D6x1000 credits in gems and metals, 3D6 M.D. weapons, 2D4 suits of M.D.C. body armor (half M.D.C. gone), 40% chance of 1D4 common magic items (no rune weapons).; attacks per melee: 9 (each head directs 3 per melee)', 'Languages: Dragonese/Elf, Dwarven, Gobbledy, plus two new languages; selects a total of four skills from Rogue, Technical (limited to languages and lore), and/or Wilderness. No skill bonuses.', 'Three heads (lion, antelope, serpent), each with its own senses: nightvision, scent-tracking, magic immunity, poison immunity, or infrared/see-invisible sight. Prowls 30%, climbs, swims well, bio-regenerates 2D6 M.D.C. per melee.', NULL, NULL, 'Necks 20 ft (6 m) head-to-trunk, 10 ft (3 m) tall at shoulder, 12-15 ft chest-to-buttock, tail 10-15 ft more; overall 50-60 ft (15.2-18.3 m) nose to tail', 'Three to four tons', '2500 years', 'Ancient ruins and lightly populated wilderness worldwide, preferring mountainous, hilly or forested regions; none currently known on Rifts Earth', 'None per se, though sometimes works with supernatural beings and magic users', 'True dragons; humans; Elves; Dwarves; Wolfen; most humanoids', 'Not applicable; a creature of brute force, not recommended as a player character', 'A savage three-headed beast - lion, antelope and serpent - bred as a weapon late in the Elf-Dwarf War; territorial and cruel.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.133-134');
  'boogie-man', 'The Boogie-Man', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but almost always evil', '{"IQ":"1D6+1","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"4D6"}', 'PE+1D6', '1D6x10', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Hit Points gain an additional 1D6 per level of experience beyond the base P.E. figure. Has no M.D.C. of its own and must acquire M.D.C. body armor.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"dodge":2}', '+4 to save vs all poisons.; attacks per melee: 4 (regardless of experience level or hand to hand combat); initiative: +2 when attacking in the dark or from behind', 'Two ancient W.P.s; Languages: Goblin/Gobbledy 98% and two others (usually human), pick two; selects a total of five skills from Rogue, Technical (limited to Rope Works, Languages, Lore), Wilderness, and any W.P.s except Heavy Weapons. No skill bonuses.', 'Nightvision 90 ft, weak daylight vision, prowls 77%, climbs 80%/70%; lures and kidnaps children, cowardly, flees stronger foes, has a sadistic sense of humor.', NULL, NULL, '2 to 3 feet tall (0.6 to 0.9 m)', '35 lbs (15.8 kg)', '600 years', 'Old cities, towns, sewers, ruins and slums worldwide; notably Chi-Town Burbs, Old Chicago, Detroit, Windsor, Iron Heart, Ciudad Juarez, Lone Star, and Washington D.C.', 'None per se, but known to associate with Goblins, Hob-Goblins, Orcs, Ghouls, and vampires', 'Humans; Elves; most humanoids', 'Most are unskilled predators; some become thieves or take a Bandit, Peasant, or Vagabond O.C.C. with half the usual number of skills; not recommended as a player character', 'A small, one-eyed, clownish predator that lures and kidnaps children, cowardly against strong foes but cruel to the helpless.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.134-135');
  'bug-bears', 'Bug Bears', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but tend selfish or evil, mostly Anarchist, Miscreant, and Diabolic', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"5D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6+2","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+30', '2D6x10', NULL, 'Hit Points (S.D.C.-world figure) gain an additional 1D6 per level of experience.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+1D6, S.D.C. 6D6+10', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":3}', '+3 to save vs magic, +3 to save vs poison/drugs, +2 to save vs Horror Factor.; dodge: +3 (+7 to strike/parry/dodge while invisible, if opponent cannot see the invisible)', 'Languages: Wolfen and Dragonese/Elven 92%, Track Animals 50%, Track Humanoids 82%, Land Navigation 82%, Identify Plants and Fruits 70%, W.P. Blunt; selects five skills from Physical (limited to Climbing, Running, Swimming, Wrestling), Rogue, Technical (limited to Languages and Lore), Wilderness, and any W.P.s except Heavy Weapons. No skill bonuses.', 'Nightvision 60 ft, sees invisible, turns invisible at will as often as it likes, can take the shape of an ordinary bear for as long as 20 minutes at a time (repeatable), teleports 40 ft about every other melee round.', 'None, other than natural abilities; radiates a magic aura similar to a Brownie (Faerie Folk)', NULL, '4 to 5 feet tall (1.2 to 1.5 m)', '150-200 lbs (67.5-90 kg)', '80 years', 'Grasslands; Ophid''s Grasslands on the Palladium World; western USA, southwestern Canada, Mongolia, and China on Rifts Earth (fewer than roughly 300 believed to exist in North America)', 'None, indifferent to all races', 'None, indifferent to all races', 'Palladium Fantasy: mostly raiders/bandits, or rough equivalent of Mercenary Fighter, Ranger, Assassin, Thief, Shaman, or Vagabond (rarely past 6th level). Rifts: Bandit, Raider, Wilderness Scout, Vagabond, or Shaman', 'A squat, furred, teddy-bear-like humanoid raider from Ophid''s Grasslands with innate invisibility, bear-shape change, and short-range teleport.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.135-136');
  'centaurs', 'Centaurs', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but mostly Principled or other good alignments', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"4D6x2"}', 'PE+1D6', '25', NULL, '4D6', NULL, 'Hit Points gain an additional 1D6 per level of experience. S.D.C. is 25 plus whatever is gained from O.C.C. and physical skills. Has no innate M.D.C.; needs custom-made M.D.C. body armor (barding) for the horse portion.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"parry":2,"dodge":3,"damage":4}', 'attacks per melee: 3 per round, or as per O.C.C. Hand to Hand training', 'Languages: Dragonese/Elven 98% (50% also literate, +15%), Faerie Speak +20%, Prowl 60%, Track animals and humanoids 77%, Wilderness Survival 88%, Land Navigation 82%; these act as instinct, and straight-percentage skills do not improve with experience.', 'Fast runner with great stamina; leaps 5 ft high or 9 ft across, farther at a run.', 'Rare; by O.C.C. only', 'Standard, roughly the same as humans', '7-8 feet (2.1-2.4 m) at the horse shoulders, about 11 feet (3.3 m) head to hoof', '800-1,100 lbs (360-495 kg)', '90 years', 'Grasslands and light forests; western plains of Canada and the U.S. on Rifts Earth; believed to have once existed in Mexico before being driven out', 'Faerie Folk; Sasquatch; Fennodi; Psi-Ponies; Simvan; traditional Native American tribes; Tundra Rangers; Justice Rangers; Cyber-Knights; people of the Colorado Baronies', 'None per se, but humans/humanoids who hunt or enslave them; Xiticix; Worm Wraiths; Slavers (mostly Splugorth); predatory plains dinosaurs; Leatherwing; Tree Spiders; monsters of the Calgary Rift', 'Palladium Fantasy: any O.C.C. but rarely magic, leaning Long Bowman, Druid, Ranger/Wilderness Scout, Mercenary/Headhunter, Scholar/Rogue Scholar, Vagabond/Peasant. Rifts: any O.C.C. except Coalition Military, robot/power armor pilot, Crazies, Juicer, or Shifter', 'A nomadic, half-human half-horse plains people, skilled hunters and archers, wary of cities but loyal once befriended.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.136-138');
  'cyber-horsemen-of-ixion', 'The Cyber-Horsemen of Ixion', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but most lean toward selfish and good alignments', '{"IQ":"2D6+8","ME":"1D6+8","MA":"1D6+12","PS":"3D6+8","PP":"3D6+8","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6+8","Spd":"7D6x2"}', 'PE+1D6', '40', NULL, '3D6', NULL, 'PS is 3D6+8 for the upper (human) body and 3D6+22 for the lower bionic horse-body; PE 2D6+12 applies to the upper body only, as the lower body is bionic. Hit Points gain +1D6 per level for the upper body. S.D.C. is 40 plus whatever is gained from physical skills. Natural Spd is 7D6x2, doubled for brief 2D4-minute spurts; bionic Spd is a fixed 220 (150 mph/240 km) for most males, 88 (60 mph/96 km) for females. M.D.C. of the lower body is by location, not a single roll: Bionic Front Legs (2) 100 each, Bionic Rear Legs (2) 160 each, Main Body (horse) 250, Upper Body (armor) 130; Bionic Barding adds 50% to these and to weight but cuts running speed 25% and makes prowling impossible.', NULL, 12, '{"initiative":3,"parry":1,"dodge":3,"disarm":1,"pull":3,"roll":1}', '+3 to save vs Horror Factor. Bionic Combat Augmentation adds +1 on initiative and +1 to strike by kick, and lets it leap 30 ft high or 70 ft across. Only 10% are full-conversion cyborgs, who carry a weapon for each bionic arm plus enhanced optics.; attacks per melee: Those gained from Hand to Hand Combat training, plus one as natural warriors; dodge: +3 when running; pull: +3 to pull punch; roll: +1 to roll with punch, fall or impact', 'Land Navigation +15%, Wilderness Survival +10%, Languages: Ixion 98% (95% also literate) plus two languages of choice (typically American, +20%), W.P. Pole Arm/Spear; all in addition to O.C.C. skills.', 'Bionic lower horse-body with location-based M.D.C.; enhanced prowl (50%+2%/level, less if bionic), strong leaping, and high running speed; bionic limbs deal Mega-Damage punches/kicks; built-in language translator and bionic lung.', 'By O.C.C. only', 'Standard, same as humans', '7-8 feet (2.1-2.4 m) at the horse shoulders, 11-12 feet (3.3-3.6 m) head to hoof', '1,800-2,400 lbs (810-1,080 kg)', '150 years, some to 220', 'Plains and light forests of southern Canada and the American West (mainly Alberta, Saskatchewan, Montana, Idaho, also Washington, Oregon, British Columbia); nomadic, avoids the Midwest and eastern regions', 'Tundra Rangers; Cyber-Knights; Justice Rangers; humans of the southwest and northwest; informally, Reid''s Rangers', 'Demons, especially at the Calgary Rift; Psi-Stalkers; Greot Hunters; Yeno; Worm Wraiths; Simvan (regard them as rivals)', 'Rifts: warriors are effectively the Cyborg O.C.C., but can be any modern O.C.C.; lean toward Headhunter, Scholar, or Adventurer', 'Technologically advanced bionic centaurs from the hidden city of Ixion, wary of the Coalition, hostile to demons, and heavily cybernetically reinforced.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.138-139');
  'chig', 'Chig - or P.P.E. Chig', 'parasite', 'rifts', 0, 'None (animal parasite)', '{"IQ":"1D4","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D4","PS":"1D6","PP":"1D6","PE":"1D6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"2D6+1"}', '2D6+2', '2D6+24', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Average P.P.E. per day drained from a host is 1D4; the P.P.E. listed is the Chig''s own reserve.', 10, 12, '{"attacks":1}', '+2 to save vs magic. Anyone seen wearing a Chig has a Horror Factor of 10 to onlookers (looks gross).', NULL, 'Siphons 1D4 P.P.E. per day from a living host; climbs rough surfaces, prowls 60%, leaps 6 ft high and 4 ft across. Host gains 98% fluency in all languages while worn.', NULL, NULL, 'About the size of a large orange', 'About the weight of a large orange', 'Three to four years', 'Wooded, grassy, dry climes; avoids hot/humid areas. Finds a host or hibernates in winter. On Rifts Earth: southwestern Canada and China.', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A tiny magical parasite resembling a flea-tick hybrid that drains PPE from a host, granting language fluency but risking mental instability over time.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.140');
  'chimera', 'Chimera', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"5D6 min 20","PP":"4D6 min 14","PE":"6D6 min 20","PB":"2D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10+10', '3D4x10', NULL, 'On an S.D.C. world: Hit Points = P.E. attribute number +30, S.D.C. = 2D4x10+10, A.R. 10.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"dodge":2,"damage":4}', 'I.Q. reflects high animal intelligence. P.S. never less than 20, P.P. never less than 14, P.E. never less than 20.', NULL, 'A predatory animal intellect, not a schemer; hunts by nipping bite, full bite, hoof kick, and a short-range gout of fire breath.', NULL, NULL, '4 ft tall at the shoulders, 10-14 ft long', '800-1200 lbs', '2,000 years', 'Deep jungles and remote hot areas; on Rifts Earth found in Africa, India, and parts of Asia.', 'none, though partially trainable by a skilled handler like a lion tamer', 'none per se, but hates good and beauty and preys on humanoids and other large mammals', NULL, 'A mega-damage lion-goat-dragon hybrid from another dimension; a predatory animal intelligence, not a schemer, prized by evil sorcerers for its potent P.P.E.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.141');
  'devil-digger', 'Devil Digger', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered to be Anarchist; animal', '{"ME":"10+1D6","MA":"6+1D6","PS":"20+1D6","PP":"10+1D6","PE":"14+1D6","PB":"6+1D6","Spd":"10+1D6"}', '6D6+12', NULL, NULL, '10', NULL, 'Horror Factor is 13 in S.D.C. settings (9 on Rifts Earth, the value given above).', 8, 9, '{"attacks":6,"parry":1,"dodge":2}', '+3 to save vs poison and magic.', NULL, 'Nightvision 90 ft, keen hearing, tracks by scent 30%, climbs 30%, swims 50%, burrows 4 ft per melee round through clay and gravel, leaps up to 4 ft.', NULL, NULL, '3-4 ft tall, 5-7 ft long', '85-200 lbs', '35 years', 'Dark, cool, subterranean dwellings; temperate and cool climates. None known to exist on Rifts Earth.', 'none per se; tolerates up to three other families sharing its territory', 'bears; feline predators; humanoids', NULL, 'A burrowing predator resembling a hyena-bear-mole hybrid with a bony horned head-plate; fiercely territorial and willing to fight intruders to the death.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.142');
  'drakin', 'Drakin (The Luck Bird)', 'magical beast', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but almost always good', '{"IQ":"2D6+1","ME":"3D6","MA":"5D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6+2","Spd":"3D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10', '1D4x10', NULL, 'Spd is x5 when flying. Non-Rifts settings: Hit Points = P.E. attribute number +12, S.D.C. = 2D4x10, A.R. 7.', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":4,"dodge":4}', 'Dodge is automatic like a parry and does not use up a melee action/attack.', 'R.C.C. Skills: Wilderness Survival 90%, Land Navigation 90%, Astronomy 70%, Track Animals 80%, Identify Plants and Fruits 70%, Demon and Monster Lore 50%, Prowl 40%, Detect Ambush (from the air) 45%, Detect Concealment (from the air) 40%, Basic Math 75%. Understands Dragonese/Elven and Wolfen 98% (not literate); can learn two more languages (+30%). Cannot speak, only squeak/whistle/shriek.', 'Flight, nightvision 220 ft, hawk-like color vision (spots a rabbit 2 miles off), sees the invisible, keen hearing (60% to notice an intruder). On Rifts Earth also senses evil/supernatural like a Psi-Stalker.', 'None, other than its own mystical nature.', 'Standard, roughly the same as humans; those with psionics may communicate via Telepathy.', '3-4 ft tall (about the size of a booted eagle)', '30-45 lbs', '300 years', 'Lightly populated forests and mountains of cool/cold climate. On Rifts Earth: Canada, northern USA, Ohio Valley, Northern Europe, New German Republic.', 'all creatures of good alignment, especially humans, Wolfen, and mutant canines', 'Feathered Death; Peryton; other creatures of evil', 'Not applicable; natural hunters and champions of good. Not recommended as a player character, but the book says it is certainly playable for an exotic choice.', 'A gentle, magical, featherless bird-like creature with leathery wings that aids good travelers; nicknamed the Luck Bird for its rumored fortune-bringing presence.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.142-143');
  'dragondactyl', 'Dragondactyl', 'beast', 'rifts', 0, 'An aggressive animal with a distinctive personality; mostly Anarchist (40%) or Miscreant (40%)', '{"IQ":"2D4","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6","PS":"2D6+10","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"2D6+10","Spd":"4D6+20"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10', '3D6', NULL, 'Spd running 4D6+20 (~30 mph); x2 for flying speed (~50-60 mph), and twice that again for a power dive. Non-Rifts settings: Hit Points = P.E. number x3 +20, S.D.C. = 3D4x10, A.R. 10.', NULL, 12, '{"initiative":2,"strike":3,"dodge":3}', 'I.Q. reflects high animal intelligence. P.S. is Supernatural on Rifts Earth. Dodge increases to +5 when flying. +4 to save vs magic, +2 to save vs Horror Factor.; attacks per melee: Males Four, Females and Young Three', NULL, 'Climbs 66%, swims 30%, prowls 66%, tracks animals 60%, nightvision 90 ft, hawk-like vision (spots a rabbit two miles off), good sense of smell, immune to all fire including magic and M.D. plasma.', NULL, NULL, '6-7 ft tall at the shoulders; 16-20 ft wingspan', '3000-5000 lbs', '800 years', 'Mountains and mountain valleys for roosting/breeding, hunts in lowlands and plains. Negligible on Rifts Earth; Splugorth breed captured Himalayan stock for Atlantis slave pens.', 'only their own kind; indifferent to all others', 'all humanoids; Perytons (rival monsters); mountain predators', NULL, 'A rare, foul-tempered, bat-winged flying steed resembling a demonic Pegasus; omnivorous and herd-forming, prized and bred by the Splugorth as a mount.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.143-145');
  'dragon-wolf', 'Dragon Wolf', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually Unprincipled (15%), Anarchist (40%), and Aberrant (25%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10', '2D4x10', NULL, 'Spd is running speed, x4 when flying. Non-Rifts settings: Hit Points = P.E. number +50, S.D.C. = 2D6x10, A.R. 12.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+2 to save vs magic. P.S. is equal to Bionic Strength.', 'Understands and speaks all languages innately, but must study and learn written languages (two of choice at +30%).', 'Shapeshifts into any humanoid form only under a full moon, reverting at first daylight; small hands with an opposable thumb let it use tools, weapons, computers, and vehicles even in wolf form.', 'Only abilities gained from a magic O.C.C.; many pursue spell casting over rituals or summoning. NPCs average 4th to 5th level.', 'Standard, roughly equivalent to humans.', 'About the size of a normal wolf, ~3.5 ft tall at the shoulders', '150-200 lbs', '1000 years', 'Moderate temperatures and forested areas, but wanders anywhere seeking adventure and magic items; fewer than a hundred believed to exist worldwide.', 'tolerates most races, including demons', 'none natural, but wary of Elves, Clergy, magic practitioners, dragons, and the supernatural', 'Palladium Fantasy: any Men of Magic, Thief, Assassin, or Mercenary Fighter. Rifts: Ley Line Walker, Mystic, Temporal Wizard, City Rat, Rogue Scholar, or Gambler most likely, but can be any Magic O.C.C., Operator, Rogue Scientist, Vagabond, Headhunter, or Mind Melter (if psychic). Uses the dragon experience table.', 'A cunning, treacherous shapeshifting predator that manipulates mortals for its own amusement, yet occasionally helps them if doing so spites a rival.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.145-146');
  'eandroth', 'Eandroth', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually Anarchist or good', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"3D6"}', 'PE+1D6', '1D4x10', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Hit Points gain an additional 1D6 per level of experience beyond the first. Armor Rating of 10 applies only in non-M.D. combat; Eandroth need M.D.C. body armor like humans to function on an M.D. battlefield.', 10, 10, '{"attacks":2}', 'attacks per melee: Two or three as simple hunters; three plus Hand to Hand skill bonuses at rogue stage', 'Language is Dragonese/Elven 98% (illiterate). Males: Land Navigation 65%, Wilderness Survival 65%, Track Animals 60%. Females: First Aid 70%, Cook 70%, Sewing 70%, Sing 50%, Skin and Prepare Animal Hides 60%.', 'Survives weeks without food or water (1D4+2 weeks); needs only a half gallon of water and two pounds of food weekly for up to two months; tolerates extreme heat but hates cold. Innate Heat Point pyrokinetic attack.', NULL, 'Males have none but the innate Heat Point. Females possess Sense Evil before the rogue change (with 2D6x10 P.P.E. and 4D6 I.S.P.), then become master psionics (Mind Mage/Mind Melter) as rogues.', '4-5 ft', '75-135 lbs', '30 years in the wilds of Palladium; longer if the Eandroth survives to become a rogue', 'Prefers extreme desert conditions on the Palladium World; rogues can be found almost anywhere.', 'none special; tend to be loners', 'none, per se', 'Palladium Fantasy: simple tribal role; the ambitious may become Mercenary Fighter, Ranger, Thief, Assassin, or Shaman as young, but an O.C.C. is usually not chosen until the rogue change, when almost any is available. Rifts: City Rat, Vagabond, or Wilderness Scout as young, with the same rule at rogue stage.', 'A reptilian, theropod-like humanoid race that matures fast, lives in small desert tribes, and undergoes a violent biological change into a tougher rogue phase after 25 years.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.146-147');
  'emirin', 'Emirin', 'animal', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually Principled (33%), Scrupulous (33%), or Unprincipled (20%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"4D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"3D6+1","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+15', '1D4x10', 'ME+3D6x10', 'Non-Rifts settings: Hit Points = P.E. number +12, S.D.C. = 1D4x10, A.R. 6. I.S.P. gains an additional 13 per level of experience; Telepathy is innate/free and I.S.P. is spent only on telepathic probes.', NULL, 8, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":3,"strike":1,"dodge":2,"pull":4,"roll":3}', '+4 to save vs Horror Factor, +2 to save vs psionic attack, all in addition to attribute bonuses. Can combine psionic attacks with physical attacks.', 'No vocal cords; understands Wolfen and Elven/Dragonese 98% (illiterate); learns new languages very quickly (three more, all at +30%); Basic Math 98%, Wilderness Survival 80%, Land Navigation 80%, Track Animals 80%, Identify Plants and Fruit 80%, Climbing 80%/50%, Swimming 80%, Fishing 60%, Holistic Medicine 50%.', 'Nightvision 60 ft (total darkness), tracks by smell 80%, identifies tracks by smell 60%, prowls 70%, recognizes poison 40%. Has no hands; manipulates objects only by Ectoplasm or Telekinesis.', NULL, 'All Emirin have Mind Mage/Mind Melter-equivalent psi-powers, leaning toward Sensitive, Healing, and Communication over combat.', '6-8 ft tall at the shoulders, about 12 ft long plus a 3 ft tail', '250-500 lbs', '80+ years', 'Mountains and dense forests on high hills; prefers mild climates with changing seasons.', 'Kankoran; Unicorns; Brownies; Nymphs; on Rifts Earth also Sasquatch, Lyn-Srial, Native American Shamans, and woodland spirits', 'none per se', 'Palladium Fantasy: Mind Mage equivalent in psionic powers, own skill list, Mind Mage experience table. Rifts: Mind Melter equivalent, own skill list, Mind Melter experience table.', 'A solitary, hand-less, giant mountain-lion-like predator that communicates purely through telepathy and defends its territory with escalating, patient cunning.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.148-150');
  'eye-killer', 'Eye Killer', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil or Anarchist', '{"IQ":"1D6+2","ME":"3D6+2","MA":"2D6","PS":"1D6+2","PP":"2D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10', '10', 'ME+100', 'P.P.E. doubles to 20 on Rifts Earth, making Eye Killers targets for Psi-Stalkers. Elsewhere (non-M.D.C.): Hit Points = P.E. number +30, S.D.C. = 6D6+6, A.R. 10. I.S.P. about that of a 4th level Mind Mage or Mind Melter.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4}', '+3 to save vs psionic attack on Rifts Earth.', 'Track Humanoids 52%, Prowl 80%, Climb 50%/25%, Swim 60%; cannot speak but understands all pre-Rifts Indian languages and Gobbledy, can learn three more; communicates by psionic Empathy and Telepathy.', 'Nightvision 120 ft, shallow burrower (2 ft per minute). Its feared killing stare is actually the psionic powers of Bio-Manipulation and Empathic Transmission, not literal magic.', NULL, 'Extensive Sensitive and Physical psionics plus Bio-Manipulation (its primary means of killing), Empathic Transmission, and (Rifts RPG) Mind Bolt; exact power list varies slightly by game edition.', '3-4 ft long, head to tail tip', '35-60 lbs', '120 years', 'Open grasslands and prairies of the American West: Nevada, Utah, Colorado, Kansas, Arizona, New Mexico, Texas, and northern Mexico.', 'evildoers of any race', 'humans and all humanoids, particularly champions of good', NULL, 'A malevolent serpent-coyote-owl hybrid whose feared death-stare is actually psionic bio-manipulation and induced fear, not a literal magical gaze.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.150');
  'feathered-death', 'Feathered Death', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but mostly evil', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"2D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', 'PE+20', 'PEx10', NULL, '3D6', NULL, 'S.D.C. gives most an equivalent of 1-2 M.D.C.; flies at 2D6x10 instead of the ground Spd.', 5, 10, '{"attacks":3,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":4}', '+2 to save vs all magic; natural A.R. only applies in S.D.C. combat.', 'Languages: Faerie Speak, Dragonese/Elven, Gobblely 90 percent plus 50 percent chance of two more at 76 percent; Land Navigation 90 percent, Wilderness Survival 90 percent, Prowl 80 percent.', 'Flight; nightvision 120 ft; keen hawk-like vision; can shapeshift into a small human at night under a full moon, reverting to bird form at first light.', 'None, but loves magic items', NULL, '16-25 inches tall (about 0.6 m)', '10-15 pounds (4.5 to 6.7 kg)', '30 years', 'Forests and low mountain regions of moderate climates', 'Coyles; Ogres; Trolls; supernatural forces of evil; loosely Orcs and Goblins', 'Faerie Folk (Sprites, Faeries, Pixies); humanoids; mutant canines; Wolfen; Kankoran; humans; Elves; Gnomes', 'Optional Palladium Fantasy Thief (thief experience table); optional Rifts Thief, Bandit or Vagabond with half the usual Related and Secondary Skills. Not recommended as a player character.', 'A small but strong bird-man with a human face who abducts, torments, and robs travelers, common only to the Palladium World.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.151');
  'grimbor', 'Grimbor', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually good or selfish', '{"IQ":"1D6+3","ME":"2D6","MA":"3D6+2","PS":"5D6","PP":"2D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"1D6+1"}', 'PE+20', '1D6x50', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'P.S. is Superhuman. Hit Points add 2D6 per level of experience. S.D.C. gives most an equivalent M.D.C. of 1-4; needs M.D.C. body armor to survive on Rifts Earth.', 6, 15, '{"attacks":4,"parry":1,"pull":2}', '+3 to save vs Horror Factor; combat-trained Grimbor get their Hand to Hand skill extra attack.', 'Palladium Fantasy (wild): dialect of Goblin 98 percent, two more languages +15 percent; males W.P. Blunt/Paired/Throwing, Identify Plants and Fruit +10 percent, Land Navigation +10 percent, Track and Trap Animals +10 percent, Skin and Prepare Animal Hides +5 percent, Swim +10 percent, Carpentry +10 percent; females W.P. Blunt, Holistic Medicine +5 percent, Identify Plants and Fruit +20 percent, Land Navigation +10 percent, Skin and Prepare Animal Hides +15 percent, Swim +10 percent, Rope Works.', 'Nightvision 40 ft; good color vision; track by smell 60 percent (males only); swim 20 percent; terrible climbers; Superhuman Strength.', NULL, NULL, '6 ft (1.8 m) bent over on knuckles, 10-12 ft (3-3.6 m) fully erect', '500 to 800 pounds (225 to 360 kg)', '60 years (Rifts)', 'Jungles and rain forests; a small tribe survives in Dinosaur Swamp, Georgia; also sold as slaves on Atlantis and found in gladiatorial arenas and Burbs', 'Tezcat (revere them as demigods); other gentle, inhuman-looking beings such as Sasquatch or Fennodi', 'Splugorth and Splugorth Slavers; humans; animal predators; human-resembling humanoids', 'Palladium Fantasy: none natively, but can be taught the equivalent of Peasant/Farmer, Ranger (no bow), or Gladiator at half Related/Secondary Skills. Rifts: basic hunter-gatherer, Vagabond, Wilderness Scout, Trapper-Woodsman, Grunt/Raider, occasionally Headhunter or Borg, at half Related/Secondary Skills; Juicer and M.O.M. conversions do not work on them.', 'A gentle, powerful ape-man race captured by the Splugorth for centuries and sold across Atlantis as slaves, laborers, and gladiators.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.151-153');
  'gromek', 'Gromek', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but seem predominantly selfish or evil', '{"IQ":"2D6+1","ME":"3D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6+2","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', 'PE+1D6', '4D6', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Flies at 6D6+6 instead of the ground Spd. S.D.C. gains more from physical skills/O.C.C. Has no natural M.D.C.; must acquire M.D.C. body armor.', 12, 14, '{"attacks":2,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"pull":2,"roll":2}', '+4 to dodge while in flight.', 'Hand to Hand: Expert (improvable), Wrestling, W.P. Sword, W.P. Blunt, W.P. Archery and Targeting, literate in native Gromek 98 percent; females also Holistic Medicine and First Aid +10 percent. A True Gromek Warrior adds another ancient W.P., two modern W.P.s, upgrades Hand to Hand, and selects Domestic/Espionage/Physical/Wilderness skills at +10 percent, using the Wilderness Scout experience table.', 'Flight; keen hawk-like vision; resistant to fire (half damage); extremely aggressive by nature.', 'By O.C.C. only (a magic-wielding Gromek is super-rare)', NULL, '8 to 10 feet (2.4 to 3 m) tall', '600 to 800 pounds (270 to 360 kg)', '180 years', 'Mountains and tall hills of moderate to hot temperature; an outpost tribe of 75-120 in the Allegheny Mountains and about 100 in the Canadian Rockies', 'occasionally Trolls or Giants', 'Humans and most intelligent life forms; Lyn-Srial and other intelligent flying humanoids (instant rivals)', 'Palladium Fantasy: any Men of Arms (especially Soldier, Knight, Paladin) or other warrior/clergy type. Rifts: any Men of Arms including military equivalents (Grunt, Commando, Ranger) except power armor, robot or vehicle pilots; also Vagabond, Rogue Scholar, City Rat, Wilderness Scout, or Hunter-Trapper; rarely a Conjurer.', 'A winged, demonic-looking alien warrior race, primitive but adaptive, that conquers territory wherever dimensional rifts strand its scouting tribes.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.153-154');
  'gruunor', 'Gruunor', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered a Miscreant evil monster, predator', '{"ME":"8+1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"20+1D6","PP":"11+1D6","PE":"20+1D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"4+1D6"}', '6D6+2', '1D4x100', NULL, '1D6', NULL, 'S.D.C. gives the equivalent of 1-4 M.D.C., but it is still damaged by S.D.C. weapons.', 16, 13, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1}', '+1 on all saving throws; nearly impervious to Horror Factor; A.R. rises to 19 when rolled into a ball; underbelly can be damaged directly (bypasses the shell) when it rears to bite.', NULL, 'Nightvision 60 ft; climbs/scales walls like a spider (90 percent/80 percent); resists fire and cold, even Mega-Damage versions, for half damage.', NULL, NULL, '4 to 6 feet (1.2 to 1.8 m) long', '80 to 110 pounds (about 45 kg)', '8 years', 'Ruins and subterranean dwellings in most climates except extreme cold; known in Old Chicago, Detroit, Windsor, and the Chi-Town Burbs', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A giant caterpillar-like insect with a false head disguising its rear stinger, curling into an armored ball when threatened.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.154-155');
  'gryphon', 'Gryphon', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Any; wild Gryphons generally Anarchist or evil, tame ones Unprincipled or Anarchist', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"4D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+50', '1D6x10', NULL, 'Flies at 1D6x10+48 instead of the ground Spd. In an S.D.C. setting: P.E.+40 Hit Points, 4D6+20 S.D.C., A.R. 9.', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":1}', '+2 on all saving throws. Three attacks per melee for a young Gryphon, four for an adult.', NULL, 'Flight; Supernatural Strength; nightvision 120 ft (total darkness); hawk-like vision (spots prey two miles away); 180-degree peripheral vision; track by sight 54 percent; prowl 66 percent; can learn up to three languages at about 50 percent understanding; instinctively hates vampires and undead.', NULL, NULL, '4 feet (1.2 m) tall at the shoulder, about 7 feet (2.1 m) long', '150 to 230 pounds (67.5 to 103.5 kg)', '200 years', 'Mountain ranges, especially coastal, and forested islands of almost any climate', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A mythical eagle-and-lion animal, prized as a trained mount and bred by Cyclops handlers for the Splugorth clients.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.155-156');
  'harpies', 'Harpies', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant (45 percent) or Diabolic (55 percent) evil only', '{"IQ":"1D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10', '1D6x10', NULL, 'Flies at 1D4x10+40 instead of the ground Spd. Normally (non-M.D.): P.E.+20 Hit Points, 2D4+20 S.D.C., A.R. 6.', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"dodge":2}', '+4 to S.D.C. damage, +2 to save vs magic, +4 to save vs poison/toxin/drugs, +2 on all magic saving throws.', NULL, 'Nightvision 90 ft (total darkness); keen color vision; poor smell; body reeks of a stench that forces a save vs nonlethal poison (16+) within 25 ft or lose half actions and suffer -2 initiative/-2 strike/-3 parry-dodge (filtered air halves the penalty, sealed air negates it); senses good or evil within 120 ft automatically, at no I.S.P. cost.', NULL, 'Standard, roughly the same as humans', '7 feet tall (2.1 m), 18 foot (5.4 m) wingspan', '200 pounds (90 kg)', '2,000 years', 'Rocky coastlines, islands, and mountain ranges, but can appear anywhere', 'sometimes Peryton, Gargoyles, and demons', 'Humanoids in general; beautiful creatures, animal or intelligent, in particular', NULL, 'A demonic, vulture-like woman-bird that hunts beauty and goodness for pleasure, fouling the air around her with a nauseating stench.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.156-157');
  'hytril', 'Hytril', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but usually Unprincipled (35 percent) or Anarchist (45 percent)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"4D6","PS":"2D6","PP":"5D6","PE":"2D6","PB":"4D6","Spd":"4D6"}', 'PE+20', '30', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Adds 1D6 Hit Points per level of experience. Speed gets +20 when leaping/swinging through tree branches. Needs custom M.D.C. body armor (about 15-25 M.D.C.) to survive Rifts Earth.', NULL, 6, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":3,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":3,"roll":5}', '+2 to save vs poison.', 'R.C.C.: Dance +5 percent, Prowl +20 percent, Acrobatics +5 percent, Climb/Rappel +20 percent, Swimming +5 percent, Concealment +4 percent, Palming +10 percent, Pick Pockets +10 percent, Pick Locks, Streetwise, Track Animals, Identify Plants and Fruits +10 percent, Land Navigation +10 percent, Wilderness Survival +10 percent, Faerie Lore, W.P. Knife or Blunt, Languages: Gobblely 98 percent plus two more at +10 percent and three more without bonus. Six Secondary Skills at level one, two more at levels 4/8/12, from a limited category list; uses the City Rat experience table.', 'Nightvision 60 ft; excellent color vision and hearing; climbs and leaps (6 ft high or 12 ft across); prehensile tail usable as a third hand.; tracks by smell 44%', NULL, NULL, 'Two and a half feet (0.76 m) tall from nose to buttocks, plus a three foot (0.9 m) tail', '25 to 40 pounds (11 to 18 kg)', '35 years, some to 70', 'Tropical and sub-tropical forests; native to the Floenry Isles, also found in the Yin-Sloth Jungles, Land of the South Winds, Atlantis, Dinosaur Swamp, and Central America', 'humans and human-like humanoids; the prettier Faerie Folk', 'Jungle predators, especially jungle cats (hunters); large or uglier humanoids (distrusted)', NULL, 'A small, thieving lemur-like tribal race fascinated with humanoids, prone to tantrums, and drawn to shiny objects.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.157-158');
  'kelpie', 'Kelpie', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant or Diabolic evil, only', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"5D6 min 22","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100', '2D6', NULL, 'Minimum P.S. of 22; Supernatural P.S. and P.E. (inflicts M.D., does not tire). Runs at 6D6+40 (also swim speed) as a horse. Normally (non-M.D.): P.E.+30 Hit Points, 3D6x10 S.D.C., A.R. 9.', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":1}', 'Underwater: +1 melee attack, +3 to strike, +4 to parry and dodge, +2 on initiative.', 'Languages: Gobblely/Goblin and Faerie Speak 98 percent, 50 percent chance of the local dominant language at 45 percent; also Faerie Lore 80 percent, Demon and Monster Lore 50 percent, Land Navigation 50 percent, Wilderness Survival 90 percent, W.P. Blunt.', 'Swimming 92%; breathes both water and air indefinitely; infrared/ultraviolet vision underwater; nightvision 30 ft; can change into a horse whenever it likes, for as long as it likes.', NULL, NULL, '6-7 feet (1.8 to 2.1 m) tall in humanoid form', '200 to 300 pounds (90 to 135 kg)', '300 years', 'Swamps, bogs, rivers, and streams of any climate, often near a ley line; especially common in England, Ireland, the New German Republic, and Europe', 'other evil Faerie Folk like Bogies, Toad Stools, Pucks, Hairy Jack, and Deadmoon Hag; the Waternix and other evil aquatic beings', 'Hates all life, especially mortals', NULL, 'A shapeshifting horse-headed water fiend that lures travelers to ride it before dragging them under to drown and devour.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.158-159');
  'ki-lin', 'Ki-Lin', 'dragon', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but almost always Principled (50 percent) or Scrupulous (40 percent)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"5D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6 min 20","PB":"5D6 min 20","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+90', '2D6x10', NULL, 'P.E. and P.B. never lower than 20; Supernatural P.S. and P.E. Flying speed 22 or 15 mph (24 km). Adds 20 P.P.E. per level if a practitioner of magic. Normally (non-M.D.): P.E.+60 Hit Points, P.E.+45 S.D.C., A.R. 14.', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+4 on all saving throws. Horror Factor is none to good beings, 14 to supernatural evil. Presence gives nearby good people +5 percent to all skills and +1 to parry/dodge while doing a good act.', 'Speaks all languages 98 percent, but must study to become literate; Faerie Lore +20 percent, Demon and Monster Lore +15 percent, Land Navigation +20 percent, Astronomy +20 percent, Basic Math +20 percent, Art +10 percent.', 'Flight; prowl 55 percent; swim 60 percent; nightvision 90 ft (total darkness); sees the invisible; turns invisible at will; resists fire and cold, even magical, for half damage; bio-regeneration 2D6 M.D.C. per melee; healing touch (2D4 Hit Points or 4D4 S.D.C.); senses evil within 120 ft.', 'Only abilities gained from a magic O.C.C.', 'Standard, roughly the same as humans', '4 feet (1.2 m) at the shoulders', '600 to 1000 pounds (270 to 450 kg)', '5000 years', 'China is its homeland, but can be found anywhere, though very rare', 'Faeries, Sprites and Faerie Folk in general; Kukulcans, dragons, and creatures of good alignment', 'Evil supernatural monsters and other forces of evil', 'May study Scholar, Healer, Druid, or any men of magic (Fantasy); or Body Fixer, Rogue Scholar, Rogue Scientist, or any practitioner of magic except Necromancy (Rifts); uses the Dragon experience table, starting at first level.', 'A gentle horse-and-dragon hybrid of good fortune from Chinese myth, drawn to help mortals in trouble despite the enmity it earns.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.159-160');
  'palladium-lizard-men', 'Palladium Lizard Men', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6"}', 'PE+12', '4D6', NULL, '2D6', NULL, 'Adds 1D6 Hit Points per level of experience. Swims twice as fast as it runs. S.D.C. gains more from O.C.C. and physical skills. Being S.D.C. creatures, they must acquire M.D.C. body armor to face Mega-Damage threats.', 9, 13, '{"initiative":1}', '+3 to save vs poison/drugs; +1 to strike and parry underwater, +2 to dodge underwater. Horror Factor 13 only applies when in an attack frenzy.', 'All speak Dragonese/Elven 98 percent natively; about a third of city-dwellers are also literate +20 percent. The Hunter/Warrior R.C.C.: Fishing +20 percent, Dance +5 percent, Play Musical Instrument +5 percent, Basic Math +5 percent, Climb +10 percent, Pilot Sail and Row Boats +10 percent, Boat Building +15 percent, Carpentry +15 percent, Hunting, Track Animals +5 percent, Skin and Prepare Animal Hides, Preserve Food +5 percent, Land Navigation +10 percent, Wilderness Survival +10 percent, Hand to Hand: Expert, two ancient W.P.s, and (on Rifts Earth) one modern W.P.; six Secondary Skills at level one, two more at levels 4/8/12.', 'Breathes underwater indefinitely; natural polarized vision; swim 90 percent.', 'By O.C.C. only', 'Standard, roughly the same as humans', 'Four and a half to five and a half feet (1.37 to 1.6 m)', '80-150 pounds (36 to 67.5 kg)', '50 years', 'Rivers, streams, swamps and lakes; the northern half of South America on Rifts Earth', 'Were-panthers', NULL, 'Palladium Fantasy: any. Rifts: any, except cyborg or formal Coalition-style military O.C.C.s. Either use the Hunter/Warrior R.C.C. skill package or select an O.C.C., but not both.', 'A semi-aquatic reptilian people who colonize waterways peacefully but mobilize an entire community to war if one of their own is harmed.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.160-161');
  'lizard-mage', 'Lizard Mage', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically Aberrant evil (70 percent), but occasionally Diabolic, Miscreant, or Anarchist', '{"IQ":"4D6 min 17","ME":"4D6 min 17","MA":"3D6","PS":"4D6 min 17","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x100+400', '5D6x100', 'MEx4', 'I.Q., M.E. and P.S. never lower than 17. Adds 2D6 per level for Hit Points. Normally (non-M.D.): P.E.+60 Hit Points, 200 S.D.C., A.R. 14.; I.S.P. +1D6 per level of experience (typically 100-200)', NULL, 17, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":4,"pull":4,"roll":2}', '+8 to save vs Horror Factor; impervious to possession; +4 to save vs all magic; +3 to circle and ward strength. Five physical or psionic attacks (or a combination), or two by magic, per melee.', 'Recognize and read runes 98 percent; recognize wards/circles 50 percent; recognize enchantments 50 percent+2 percent/level; recognize magic items 62 percent+2 percent/level; recognize precious metals/stones 80 percent.', 'Keen vision; sharp hearing; warm-blooded.', 'Palladium Fantasy: knows all power words, mystic symbols, wards, all Circles of Protection, and 1D6+1 circles each of Summoning and Power, plus spells from their magic O.C.C.s (typical NPC knows eight spells per level 1-8, three per level 9-15). Rifts: knows all power words and most mystic symbols, reads runes, and can use Techno-Wizard devices; may be a Temporal Wizard, Temporal Warrior, Stone Mage, or Bio-Wizard (Bio-Wizard is never a player character).', 'A limited Master psychic: all Sensitive and Physical powers, five Healing powers, and the Super-Psionics Bio-Manipulation and Bio-Regeneration (M.D.C.) plus two others of choice', '7-8 feet (2.1 to 2.4 m)', '250-350 pounds (112.5 to 157.5 kg)', '18,000 years on Rifts Earth; normally 180 to 400 years', 'Anywhere', 'Evil creatures of magic and supernatural forces; uses humans and other intelligent beings as pawns', 'Elves and Dwarves (a lasting enmity)', NULL, 'An ancient, egotistical reptilian sorcerer-lord who craves knowledge and power, once ruling the Palladium World Age of Chaos.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.161-163');
  'loogaroo', 'Loogaroo', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil (any) or Anarchist; most wicked', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"3D6+2","PP":"2D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10', '2D4x10', NULL, 'Spd is 2D6 running or 1D4x10+20 flying; the HP/SDC/AR figures given are the non-Rifts (SDC) form; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+50, S.D.C. 2D4x10, A.R. 6', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"strike":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+4 to parry/dodge when airborne; +6 save vs Horror Factor and possession; +3 save vs all magic; impervious to poison; impervious to S.D.C. weapons except silver (does equivalent M.D.); Turn Dead spells and the clergy ability do not repel it, whatever its undead reputation', 'Speaks Dragonese/Elven, Dwarf, Gobblely/Goblin, and one other (usually human) at 95%; 80% literate in Dragonese/Elven and Dwarven 95%; Land Navigation 95%', 'Flies; nightvision 90 ft; sees invisible; hawk vision spots carrion 2 miles off; turns invisible at will; senses magic within a mile and good within 600 ft; immune to poison', 'None, unless of a magic O.C.C. (6th-10th level)', NULL, '5-6 feet (1.5-1.8 m)', '250-300 lbs (112.5-135 kg)', '900 years', 'Ancient ruins, deserts, plains, wastelands, and light forests; roosts in ruined cities on Rifts Earth', 'Goblins; Orcs; Ogres; evil people of every variety', 'Humans; Elves; canine races; champions of good', 'Palladium Fantasy: Thief, Assassin, Wizard, Warlock, Diabolist, Summoner, or evil priest. Rifts: Line Walker, Mystic, Shifter, Necromancer, Warlock, Vagabond-Mage, Vagabond-Thief, Bandit, Raider, Vagabond, or Wilderness Scout; never Techno-Wizard or Bio-Wizard. Not recommended as a player character.', 'Giant vulture-like scavenger, reputedly an undead witch, that preys on the weak and feeds on the dead in wastelands.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.163-164');
  'manticore', 'Manticore', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but usually Miscreant (45%) or Diabolic (45%)', '{"IQ":"1D4+2","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+16","PP":"2D6+10","PE":"3D6+12","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6+12"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+40', '3D6', NULL, 'PPE is 3D6 even though only a minor creature of magic; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 4D6+40, S.D.C. 2D4x10, A.R. 8', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":3,"parry":4,"dodge":4}', 'Supernatural P.S.; +5 save vs poison; +6 save vs Horror Factor', 'Speaks Dragonese/Elf 98% and can learn 1D4 other languages (+10%)', 'Nightvision 60 ft, prowl 50%, swim 50%, climb 30%, tracks by smell 52%, leaps 20 ft high or long', NULL, NULL, '8-10 feet long (2.4-3 m), 4 feet (1.2 m) tall at shoulders', '600-700 lbs (270-315 kg)', '400 years', 'Grasslands, savannas, steppes, wastelands, occasionally light forests/ruins; warm to hot climates; rare on Rifts Earth', 'Forces of evil', 'Humans; Elves; generally all humanoids', NULL, 'Solitary lion-bodied predator with a poisonous barbed tail and a human face that stalks humanoids and large game.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.164');
  'maxpary', 'Maxpary', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but most (88%) Anarchist', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"4D6 min 17","PP":"2D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+40', '1D4x10', NULL, 'P.S. never less than 17 (Superhuman); HP figure is P.E. +1D6, gaining another +1D6 per level of experience; is M.D.C. on Rifts Earth; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+1D6, S.D.C. 50, A.R. 13', NULL, 13, '{"initiative":1}', 'Superhuman P.S.; +8 save vs poison, toxins, and drugs', 'Hand to Hand: Basic, Climb 60%/50%, Carpentry 50%, Land Navigation 80%, Wilderness Survival 50%, W.P. Sword, W.P. Knife, W.P. Blunt; can use scavenged Vibro-Blades and basic energy weapons', 'Nightvision 90 ft, excellent dim-light vision, poor day vision 20 ft, keen hearing, digs 10 ft/minute, holds breath 20 minutes, resists toxic fumes', 'A few may be Warlocks (Earth or Air) or a Shaman', NULL, '4-5 feet (1.2-1.5 m)', '250-300 lbs (112.5-135 kg)', NULL, 'Underground complexes, especially pre-Rifts ruins; scattered colonies worldwide, notably infesting the New German Republic', 'None; keep to themselves', 'None per se; anyone who invades their lair', 'Palladium Fantasy and Rifts: mostly Soldiers (50%) or Peasant/Worker Drones (48%), about 2% Warlock or Shaman.', 'Subterranean humanoid from another dimension that farms alien fungus in tunnels and fiercely defends its lair.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.164-165');
  'maxpary-shambler', 'Maxpary Shambler', 'undead', 'rifts', 0, 'Anarchist, but effectively evil to all non-Maxpary', '{"IQ":"4","ME":"12","MA":"1","PS":"26","PP":"10","PE":"N/A","PB":"3","Spd":"10"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6+70', '1D4', NULL, 'As a zombie has a combined 3D4x10 Hit Points/S.D.C. on S.D.C. worlds; is M.D.C. on Rifts Earth; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 3D4x10, A.R. 14', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":4}', 'Supernatural P.S.; +11 damage to S.D.C. attacks; impervious to Horror Factor, possession, and all mental/physical attacks except magic and fire', NULL, 'Bio-regenerates 2D6 M.D.C. per melee; regrows severed limbs/heads in 24 hours unless burned; immune to non-magical weapons including M.D. energy weapons and Vibro-Blades; senses prey supernaturally; cannot cross holy water or fire', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Indefinite, until completely destroyed', NULL, NULL, 'All life forms except living Maxpary', NULL, 'Undead zombie a slain Maxpary rises as, mindlessly defending the tribe''s tunnels until burned to ash.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.165-166');
  'melech', 'Melech', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but typically Anarchist (30%), Miscreant (30%), Diabolic (27%), Aberrant (11%), 2% other', '{"IQ":"1D6+1","ME":"2D6+1","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6+2","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"5D6x2"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+40', '3D6', NULL, 'In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+12, S.D.C. 1D6x10+30, A.R. 9', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":5,"strike":3,"parry":3,"dodge":4}', '+2 S.D.C. damage; +2 on all saving throws; impervious to poison/drugs', 'Speaks Dragonese/Elven and Gobblely/Goblin 90%, may know 1D4 others; Wilderness Survival 80%, Land Navigation 80%, Track Humanoids 35%, Track Animals 45%, Swim 40%, Climb 20%/10%, W.P. Knife plus two W.P.s of choice', 'Nightvision 60 ft, sees invisible, keen hearing, tracks blood scent 65%, leaps 20 ft high or 40 ft across, impervious to poison', NULL, NULL, '8 feet (2.4 m) at the shoulders, 18-20 feet (5.5-6.1 m) to the top of the head', '1200-2000 lbs (540-900 kg)', '200 years', 'Desolate, sparsely populated areas from northern steppes to jungles; on Rifts Earth found in Atlantis and parts of Europe', 'Giants; vampires; demons; creatures of evil intent', 'Humanoids; all creatures of a good alignment', NULL, 'Demonic horse-and-dinosaur hybrid from the Yin-Sloth Jungles that tortures captives and hoards small treasures.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.167');
  'mucker', 'Mucker', 'demon', 'rifts', 0, 'Rare Anarchist at best; mostly Miscreant (40%) or Diabolic (55%)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"2D4+19","PP":"2D6+14","PE":"1D6+17","PB":"1D4","Spd":"6D6+15"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+70', '2D6x10', NULL, 'May wear additional body armor; Horror Factor is treated as 13 by those who know about Muckers; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx3, S.D.C. PE+50, A.R. 14', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":3,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":5,"pull":5,"disarm":4,"roll":3}', 'Supernatural P.S.; +5 save vs Horror Factor; any spell cast on a Mucker has a 1-3% chance to reflect back onto the caster; Vulnerable: silver-plated weapons do M.D. +50%; holy weapons do double damage', 'Magically understands/speaks all languages 95%; Climb 85%/80%, Land Navigation 80%, Track Humanoids 56%, Concealment 90%, Palming 80%, Pick Locks 70%, Prowl 60%, Use & Recognize Poison 70%, Recognize Weapon Quality 65%, Escape Artist 60%, Basic Math 90%', 'Nightvision 300 ft; needs no food or drink; rarely fatigues; bio-regenerates 2D6 M.D.C. per melee; resists fire/cold/electricity; immune to mind control and magical sleep/paralysis; leaps 30-45 ft', NULL, NULL, '3-4 feet (0.9-1.2 m)', '200-300 lbs (90-135 kg)', 'Effectively immortal, though can be slain in combat', 'Land of the Damned and Northern Hinterlands on the Palladium World; regions infested by demonkind on Rifts Earth (Calgary Rift, Detroit-Windsor Rift, Magic Zone, Germany, Russia, China)', 'None for long, though may join other evil, power-hungry beings for large-scale destruction', 'Everyone, especially those who cross or oppose them', NULL, 'Malicious imp-like demon that ambushes travelers for sport and can only be controlled by learning its secret true name.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.167-169');
  'owl-thing', 'Owl-Thing', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but usually considered Anarchist or Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D4+1","ME":"5D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"1D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"2D6","PB":"3D6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6', '4D6', 'MEx5', 'Spd doubles in flight, but flight can only be sustained 2D4+2 minutes before needing to rest; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+10, S.D.C. 1D4x10', NULL, 11, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"dodge":3}', NULL, 'Own code of chirps, hoots, howls and whistles; 60% understand and speak (in a shrill voice) one humanoid language, usually Gobblely or Dragonese', 'Nightvision 120 ft; hawk-like vision spots a trinket 2 miles off; tracks by sight 75%/smell 60%; prowl 64%; pick pockets 35%; limited, short-duration flight', NULL, 'I.S.P. is M.E. x5: Presence Sense, Sixth Sense/Sense Traps, Resist Fatigue, Resist Thirst, Bio-Regeneration, Telepathy/Commune with Animals, Empathy, limited Telekinesis; strength equal to a 4th level Mind Mage or Mind Melter', '2.5-3.5 feet (about 0.9 m)', '20-30 lbs (9-13.5 kg)', '50 years', 'Grasslands and desert areas of the northern Palladium World wastelands; none confirmed on Rifts Earth except perhaps Atlantis', 'Other animals it psionically befriends, especially feline predators, to guard its nest', 'Canine and feline predators', NULL, 'Small psychic, owl-like scavenger that hoards shiny trinkets and psionically befriends larger beasts for protection.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.169');
  'pegasus', 'Pegasus', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but usually good; Principled (50%) or Scrupulous (45%)', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"5D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"4D6","Spd":"5D6"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10', '2D4x10', 'MEx6', 'Spd is x5 in flight; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+30, S.D.C. 1D6x10+10', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":2,"strike":1,"parry":1,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', '+4 to dodge in flight; +1 save vs poison and disease', NULL, 'Flies, soars/hovers; hawk-like vision spots prey 3 miles off; nightvision 90 ft; tracks by sight 45%; leaps 20 ft across/10 ft high, soaring leap 100 ft; superhuman strength and endurance', NULL, 'I.S.P. is M.E. x6: Sense Evil, Empathy, limited Telepathy', '6-7 feet (1.8-2.1 m) at shoulder, wingspan 20-30 feet (6-9 m)', '1000-1200 lbs (450-540 kg)', '100 years', 'Extremely high, rugged mountains; prefers moderate to cold temperatures', NULL, 'Splugorth and their minions; Peryton; Loogaroo', NULL, 'Rare winged horse descended from escaped Atlantean stock; fears humanoids but can be a loyal trained mount.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.169-170');
  'peryton', 'Peryton (Demon Deer)', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant (40%) or Diabolic (60%) evil', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"2D6+12","PP":"2D6+8","PE":"2D6+8","PB":"4D6 min 17","Spd":"22"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10+10', '3D6', NULL, 'P.B. never less than 17; Spd is 22 running, 44 (30 mph/48 km) flying; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+6D6, S.D.C. 2D4x10, A.R. 10', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2,"roll":2}', 'Supernatural P.S.; +4 dodge in flight; +6 save vs Horror Factor', 'Language of whines and whistles; can learn the basics of two languages like a horse or dog (60% comprehension)', 'Exceptional long-range vision like a Pegasus; nightvision 90 ft; tracks by sight 77%; prowl 40%; swim 60%; climb 40%; leaps 15 ft across/10 ft high, soaring leap 100 ft; impervious to S.D.C. weapons including silver, fire, and cold', NULL, NULL, '5 feet (1.5 m) at the shoulder, wingspan about 20 feet (6.1 m)', '240-340 lbs (108-153 kg)', '300 years', 'Mountainous areas near oceans and seas; eastern coast of Europe, England, and Atlantis', NULL, 'All humanoids; Pegasus; rivals Dragondactyls', NULL, 'A demonic flying deer whose shadow resembles a man; hunts humanoids and rival flying beasts such as Pegasus.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.170-171');
  'ratling', 'Ratling', 'humanoid', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but most NPCs are selfish or evil', '{"IQ":"4D6","ME":"2D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"2D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"3D6"}', 'PE+1D6', '4D6', NULL, '1D6', NULL, 'HP is P.E. +1D6 per level of experience; S.D.C. is 4D6 plus O.C.C./physical skill points; no innate M.D.C. - Ratlings must acquire body armor, magic, or a force field for M.D.C. protection', NULL, 11, NULL, NULL, 'Palladium RPG Ratlings speak Western Human dialect, Gobblely/Goblin, and Dwarven at 98% (25% literate); Rifts Ratlings speak Gobblely 98% plus one other language (a third literate in an Earth language); also Underground Tunneling 30%+5%/level, Underground Architecture 20%+5%/level, Underground Sense of Direction 40%+5%/level', 'Keen color vision; nightvision 40 ft; passive nightvision to 1200 ft with a light source; poor day vision 90 ft; sensitive whiskers halve blind/dark penalties; keen hearing; climb 70%, swim 70%, imitate voices 60% (instinctive)', 'By O.C.C. only', 'Standard', '4-5.5 feet tall (1.2-1.65 m)', '45-90 lbs (20-40.5 kg)', '55 years', 'Subterranean cities and ancient tunnel systems beneath the Western Empire of the Palladium World', 'None per se, but may join adventurers or beneficial associates', 'Everyone; they trust no one; especially Changelings and other shape shifters', 'Palladium Fantasy: any, leaning Mercenary Fighter, Thief, Assassin, Wizard, Warlock, Shaman. Rifts: any except Coalition Military, leaning City Rat, Operator, Vagabond, Juicer, ''Borg, Headhunter, Ley Line Walker, Mystic, Techno-Wizard.', 'Cowardly, rat-like humanoid race of skilled tunnelers and thieves who secretly dwell beneath Western Empire cities.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.171-172');
  'sandwyrm', 'Sandwyrm', 'dragon', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but usually Anarchist (30%), Miscreant (30%), or Diabolic (35%)', '{"IQ":"1D6+4","ME":"1D6+6","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"6D6+30","PP":"1D6+8","PE":"1D6+22","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6+30"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x1000', '6D6', 'ME', 'PS is Supernatural. hp/sdc are adult figures per the book''s multiply-by-ten instruction (young: HP PEx2+100, SDC 1D6x100); mdc given is adult (young mdc is PEx2). A.R. 12 young/15 adult (adult used). Spd is halved when digging or traveling underground. PPE grows +3D6 per level of experience beyond the base 6D6. ISP grows +1D6 per level of experience beyond the ME base.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx20+1000, S.D.C. 1D6x1000, A.R. 15', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":6}', 'Hatchling/Young: +1 initiative, +2 strike, +2 parry, automatic dodge, +1 pull punch, +2 all saves, +4 save vs possession, +6 save vs Horror Factor; all doubled for adults. Vulnerable to rune weapons (double damage) and tends to underestimate opponents.', 'Underground skills roughly equal to Dwarves (no actual building); Climb 80%/75%, Land Navigation 80%, Track Animals 70%, Track Humanoids 65%, Wilderness Survival 90%; speaks a guttural form of Gobblely and Dragonese/Elven 75%.', 'Supernatural strength and endurance, digs and burrows underground, tracks by smell 70% (+15% on a blood trail), nightvision 600 feet, sees invisible, quarter damage from magic fire, bio-regenerates 6D6 M.D.C. per melee.', 'Two spells per level of experience chosen from level 1-4 Fire or Earth Warlock spells; may mix both lists but only one list per pick', 'Empathy, Presence Sense, Mind Block, plus 1D4 Sensitive powers of choice', '300-400 feet long, 40-50 feet tall', NULL, 'Estimated at 1000 years', 'Baalgor Wastelands only; not believed to exist on Rifts Earth', 'Rarely, other dragons, powerful sorcerers, demon lords, demigods, gods and similar beings', 'Virtually everything', NULL, 'Immense sand-dwelling proto-dragon of the Baalgor Wasteland; ambushes prey from beneath dunes using tentacled jaws, fire breath, and crude Warlock magic.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.172-173');
  'scarecrows', 'Scarecrows', 'construct', 'rifts', 0, 'Evil, typically Aberrant (30%), Miscreant (40%), or Diabolic (28%); rare Anarchist', '{"IQ":"2D6+2","ME":"3D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+1","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100+200', '4D6', NULL, 'hp/sdc/A.R. of 6 are the non-Mega-Damage figures; on Rifts Earth the Scarecrow uses the M.D.C. figure instead. PPE is increased by whatever a magic O.C.C. grants. About 44% have latent psionics but no ISP formula is printed; determine as usual.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+20, S.D.C. 1D4x50+100, A.R. 6', NULL, 15, NULL, '+1 initiative, +4 S.D.C. damage, +2 strike/parry/dodge, +3 save vs magic; impervious to poison, drugs, gases; doesn''t need to breathe. Fighting headless: all combat bonuses halved, initiative lost. Only fire can destroy one; Mega-Damage fire (plasma, incendiary, magic fire) does double damage.; attacks per melee: Per hand to hand combat training, plus one per melee round; or two by magic', 'Typically two O.C.C.s: primary at 1D6+4 level, secondary at 1D4+2 level; needs double normal experience per level; typical level 8th in at least one O.C.C.', 'Impervious to cold, heat, poison, and body-affecting magic (paralysis, blind, mute, aging, disease, life drain); supernatural regeneration, 1D4x10 M.D.C. every five minutes, full reform in 12 hours.', 'By O.C.C. only', 'About 44% have latent psychic powers (Major psionic in Rifts); determine as usual, or may become a Mystic', '6 feet tall', '30-80 pounds', 'Effectively immortal until destroyed by fire; average age 3D6x100', 'Anywhere; not known to exist on Rifts Earth; most common in the Eastern Territory of the Palladium World', 'None per se; any alliance is a union of convenience', 'None, per se', 'Palladium Fantasy: any except Priest, Witch, or Shaman (must meet O.C.C. attribute requirements); Rifts: any, but avoids medical/mechanical O.C.C.s, favoring Men at Arms, Scholars, Adventurers, and especially magic (many are Mystics)', 'Animated straw constructs made by a lost Diabolist ritual; nearly indestructible except by fire, and some pursue multiple classes and sorcery.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.173-175');
  'scorpion-devil', 'Scorpion Devil', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered an evil animal predator', '{"IQ":"1D4","ME":"3D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+10","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+6","PB":"1D4","Spd":"2D6+10"}', '6D6', '2D4x10', NULL, '2D4', NULL, 'Though an S.D.C. creature, a typical one survives a single point of M.D.', 6, 10, '{"attacks":4}', '+4 initiative, +2 strike/parry, +4 dodge, +3 roll with impact, +8 save vs Horror Factor; no penalty for being blinded or in total darkness.', NULL, 'Nearsighted beyond 3-4 feet but has near-supernatural smell and hearing; Prowl 30%, Climb 52%, Track by smell 90%, Swim 25%.', NULL, NULL, '2 feet tall, 3.6 feet long', '35-50 pounds', '15 years', 'Wilderness areas with light forests, caves and ruins', NULL, 'Humanoids and other forest predators', NULL, 'Small, nearly blind predator with keen smell and hearing that attacks boldly despite its size, delivering a paralyzing-strength poison sting.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.175');
  'shadow-stalker', 'Shadow Stalker', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Aberrant (65%), Miscreant (10%), Diabolic (10%), Anarchist (15%)', '{"IQ":"1D6+6","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"1D6+6","PS":"2D6+10","PP":"3D6+7","PE":"4D6+8","PB":"2D6","Spd":"6D6"}', NULL, NULL, '70', '2D6x10+PE', NULL, 'hp/sdc are the non-Mega-Damage figures; on Rifts Earth it uses the 70 M.D.C. figure instead.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 46, S.D.C. 22, A.R. 10', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5}', '+4 initiative, +4 strike, +2 parry/dodge, +8 save vs Horror Factor. Weakness: all attributes, M.D.C., skill ratios, bonuses and abilities are halved in daylight (including magically summoned sunlight); spell duration/range/damage also halved in sunlight.; attacks per melee: Five physical or two by magic', 'Invisible in shadow/darkness, Prowl in shadows or darkness 90%, Climb/Scale Walls 80%/70%, Land Navigation 60%, Track Humanoids 40%, Wilderness Survival 80%.', 'Bio-regenerates 2D6 M.D.C. per melee round (every 15 seconds); innately knows if a spell caster has ever summoned a Shadow Beast to service.', 'All Wizard spells levels 1-2 plus 1D4+4 spells from levels 3-5, or full Shadow Magic plus 1D6 Wizard spells levels 1-2; cast at 4th level proficiency, halved in daylight', NULL, 'Seven feet tall', '200-300 pounds', 'Effectively immortal', 'Anywhere; most common in the Land of the Damned', 'Shadow Beasts and a few others', 'Any intelligent humanoids, especially Summoners, Shifters, or slavers', 'None available; automatically equivalent to a 4th level Wizard/Line Walker', 'Black humanoid silhouette from the Dimension of Shadows that hunts anyone who has ever summoned a Shadow Beast; badly weakened by daylight.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.175-176');
  'silonar', 'Silonar', 'animal', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered Anarchist or Miscreant', '{"IQ":"1D4","ME":"1D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"22+1D6","PP":"18+1D6","PE":"20+2D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"34+4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6x10', '2D6', NULL, 'hp/sdc/A.R. 10 are the S.D.C.-world figures; on Rifts Earth it uses the 3D6x10 M.D.C. figure instead. Minimum speed is 38 (26 mph); most have a speed of 44-55.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 6D6+14, S.D.C. 4D6+40, A.R. 10', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":4}', '+1 initiative, +1 strike/parry, +3 dodge, +6 save vs psionic attack (too stupid), +12 save vs Horror Factor (fearless and stupid).', NULL, 'Runs 10 hours without exhaustion, leaps 20 feet long/10 feet high, survives a week without food or water, smells blood a mile away, tracks blood scent 55%; frenzies at the scent of blood or sight of combat.', NULL, NULL, '8-9 feet tall at the shoulders', '400-800 pounds', '50 years', 'Deserts and grasslands; cannot survive climates below 40 degrees F for long (3D4 days of constant cold kills it); on Rifts Earth found west of the Rocky Mountains (Nevada, Utah, Arizona, western Colorado, Idaho, Northern Mexico, parts of California)', NULL, 'Large predators and humanoids', NULL, 'Stubborn, foul-tempered velociraptor-like riding beast bred by the Eandroth; bites its own rider and turns savage at the scent of blood.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.176-177');
  'spectre', 'Spectre', 'undead', 'rifts', 0, 'Typically Miscreant (45%) or Diabolic (45%), occasionally Anarchist (10%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"20+2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6","PP":"2D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PEx5', '50+2D6', '90', 'hp/sdc/A.R. 14 are the non-Mega-Damage figures; the PE-x5 M.D.C. figure applies instead, and the Spectre is otherwise invulnerable to poison, drugs, and ordinary/Mega-Damage weapons. Spd shown is running; flying speed is 22 (15 mph/24 km). I.S.P. of 90 is doubled to 180 on Rifts Earth.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+20, S.D.C. 2D6+12, A.R. 14', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":2}', '+2 strike and dodge; invulnerable to all normal and Mega-Damage weapons - only magic and psionics can harm it.; attacks per melee: Two physical and one psionic per melee, or four psionic attacks per melee', NULL, 'Flies at speed 22, changes size at will (6-15 feet), heals twice as fast as a human, whole-body astral projection without leaving its body behind.', NULL, 'I.S.P. 90 (doubled to 180 on Rifts Earth); power equal to a 4th level Mind Mage or Mind Melter. First Edition style: all levels 1-3 psionics. Rifts/2nd Edition style: all Sensitive and Physical psionics plus Detect Psionics, Bio-Regeneration, Bio-Manipulation, Hypnotic Suggestion, Mind Block Auto-Defense, Mind Bolt.', '6-15 feet, changes shape/size at will', 'Approximately 100 pounds regardless of size', 'Unknown - possibly immortal', 'Virtually any location on Earth and other dimensions, avoiding extreme cold or heat', 'Evil supernatural forces, particularly very powerful beings', 'Humanoids and forces of good', NULL, 'Malevolent humanoid energy ghost immune to physical and mega-damage weapons, vulnerable only to magic and psionics; can astrally project at will.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.177-178');
  'sphinx', 'Sphinx', 'monster', 'rifts', 1, 'Any, but tend to be Principled (20%), Scrupulous (25%), Unprincipled (20%) or Anarchist (12%)', '{"IQ":"4D6","ME":"4D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"5D6","PP":"4D6","PE":"5D6","PB":"5D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '6D6x10', '3D4x10', NULL, 'P.S. is Supernatural on Rifts Earth. Spd is running; x5 for flight. A.R. 10 applies in S.D.C. settings. P.P.E. is a natural base of 3D4x10 plus P.P.E. gained from a magic O.C.C. (divided by half). Psionics are Standard, roughly the same as humans, with no ISP formula printed.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+60, S.D.C. 5D6x5, A.R. 10', NULL, 17, '{"attacks":4}', '+2 initiative, +3 strike/parry/dodge, +4 dodge in flight, +2 roll with punch or impact, +4 pull punch, +2 on all saving throws.', 'Magically speaks all languages 98%; literate in Dragonese/Elven 98% plus four others of choice 92%; Math Basic & Advanced 98%, Anthropology 75%, Computer Operation 90%, Sing 85%, Write 85%, Art 85%; plus 12 additional secondary skills. Average Level of O.C.C. Experience: NPCs 1D6+1, PCs 1D4 (double XP needed per subsequent level).', 'Never tires while flying, nightvision 120 feet (absolute darkness), keen night-sight (1/6 normal light needed), hawk-like vision (spots a book 2 miles off), Prowl 60%, Track by sight 77%, Swim 40%; leaps 30 feet normal or 200 feet flight-assisted.', 'May study any form of magic, particularly Wizard, Ley Line Walker, Mystic, Temporal Wizard, Stone Master, or Techno-Wizardry', 'Standard, roughly the same as humans', '5 feet tall, 8-10 feet long plus tail', '1500-1800 pounds', '2,000+ years', 'Unknown; found throughout the Palladium World, particularly the southern hemisphere', 'Faerie Folk and champions of good', 'Supernatural evil and slavers', 'R.C.C. Sphinx, Master of Magic and Knowledge (Rifts); then selects a scholarly or magical O.C.C. from Rifts or Palladium Fantasy (or Body Fixer, Cyber-Doc, City Rat/Hack Rat, Operator, Rogue Scholar, Rogue Scientist, Preacher, Gambler, or Vagabond) - only that O.C.C. skills are gained, not secondary/other skills', 'Winged lion-eagle-human scholar-adventurer craving luxury and knowledge, sometimes posing as a religious figurehead before abandoning failed worshippers.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.178-179');
  'syvan', 'Syvan', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Selfish or evil', '{"IQ":"3D6+1","ME":"14+2D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"3D6+1","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x100', '1D4x10', 'MEx10', 'hp/sdc/A.R. 13 are the non-Mega-Damage figures; on Rifts Earth it uses the 1D4x100 M.D.C. figure instead.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx10, S.D.C. 3D4x10, A.R. 13', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":4}', '+1 strike, +2 parry/dodge, +3 roll with impact, +3 save vs psionics, +2 save vs all magic.; attacks per melee: Four physical or five psionic', 'Horsemanship +20%, Prowl +10%, Play a Musical Instrument +10%, Dragonese/Elven 98% (literate), plus four additional languages +15%; may select 11 more skills from Communications/Domestic/Espionage/Military/Pilot/Pilot Related/Rogue/Technical/W.P. at a proficiency equal to its psionic level (1D6+4). Average Level of Experience: 1D6+4.', 'Sees the invisible, nightvision 90 feet (total darkness), recognizes and is immune to illusions 90%; senses emotions at 80% accuracy and detects the supernatural like a Psi-Stalker.', NULL, 'I.S.P. M.E.x10; proficiency equal to a 1D6+4 level Mind Mage or Mind Melter. First Edition style: all psi-abilities levels 1-6. Rifts/2nd Edition style: all Healing, Sensitive, and Physical psionics plus Bio-Regeneration (M.D.C.), Bio-Manipulation, Empathic Transmission, Electrokinesis, Telekinesis (Super), Telekinetic Force Field, Mentally Possess Others, Mind Block Auto-Defense, Mind Bond, Mind Wipe, Psi-Shield, Psi-Sword', '6-7 feet tall', '160-200 pounds', 'Immortal - lives until destroyed', 'Found in all environments', 'None per se, though may grow fond of favorite pawns', 'All intelligent life', NULL, 'Secretive half-decayed manipulator who rules through puppet leaders from the shadows, wielding deception, illusions, and Mind Melter-level psionics.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.179-180');
  'unicorn', 'Unicorn', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Principled (50%) and Scrupulous (50%)', '{"IQ":"8","ME":"2D6+2","MA":"2D6+2","PS":"18+2D6","PP":"18+2D6","PE":"14+2D6","PB":"18+2D6","Spd":"40+6D6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x100', '4D6x10', 'MEx10', 'I.Q. is given in words (very high animal intelligence, about a human 8), so no formula. hp/sdc/A.R. 7 are the non-Mega-Damage figures; on Rifts Earth it uses the 1D6x100 M.D.C. figure instead.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+50, S.D.C. 3D6x10, A.R. 7', NULL, 10, '{"attacks":4}', '+4 initiative, +1 strike/parry/dodge, +4 pull punch/kick, +2 roll with impact, +3 on all saving throws, +5 save vs Horror Factor.', 'Magically understands all languages (but is illiterate); communicates telepathically and empathically; Basic Math 80%, Land Navigation 98%, Wilderness Survival 90%, Identify Plants 85%, Holistic Medicine 50%.', 'Exceptional running speed, never tires, resists cold (half damage), nightvision 90 feet (total darkness); on Rifts Earth leaps 50 feet high or 100 feet long from a gallop.', 'None, other than its own being', 'I.S.P. M.E.x10; automatic Sense Evil, Sense Magic, and Sixth Sense (no I.S.P. cost); plus Empathy, Telepathy (limited), Mind Block, and Psychic Purification (must touch the victim with its horn)', '4-6 feet at the shoulder', '400-700 pounds', '10,000 years', 'The deepest forests, usually of temperate or cool climes', 'Faerie Folk, Drakin, champions of light, other creatures of good alignment', 'Peryton, Loogaroo, demons, and all evil creatures', 'None - animal; not recommended as a player character, but possible at G.M. discretion', 'Good-aligned, horse-like psychic beast that senses evil, shuns wicked or impure beings, and befriends only the innocent or truly virtuous.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.180-181');
  'weirdwing', 'Weirdwing', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but usually Unprincipled (30%), Anarchist (35%) or Aberrant (15%)', '{"IQ":"2D6+5","ME":"2D6+6","MA":"2D6+7","PS":"1D6+6","PP":"3D6+4","PE":"2D6+3","PB":"2D6","Spd":"3D6+23"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+30', '6D6', '3D6x10', 'Spd is 3D6+23 flying or 1D6+2 walking. I.S.P. gains +10 per level of experience beyond the base roll. A.R. of 5 applies only in S.D.C. settings; on Rifts Earth it is an M.D.C. creature instead.; I.S.P. +10 per level of experience; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PEx4, S.D.C. 3D6+30, A.R. 5', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"dodge":3}', '+1 strike, +3 dodge, +2 all saving throws.; attacks per melee: 3 physical or 4 psionic per melee', 'Skill equivalents: Anthropology +20%, Astronomy & Navigation +20%, Basic Math +20%, Art +10%, History +20%, Lore: Demons and Monsters +20%, Lore: Religion +15%, Lore: Magic +10%, Read Elven and 1D4 languages +15% to literacy, Escape Artist +5%, Pick Locks +10%; magically understands all languages and speaks a bizarre tongue anyone understands.', 'Bat/bird/cat hybrid with leathery wings, prehensile tail for hanging and grabbing, and opposable-thumbed claws; phenomenal memory; Special Super-Clairvoyance reveals a named individual''s past, present state, and glimpses of their future.', NULL, 'Master Psychic: all Sensitive powers, Detect Psionics, Exorcism, Lust for Life, Psychic Diagnosis, Advanced Trance State, Death Trance, Float, Impervious to Cold, Impervious to Fire, Resist Fatigue, Mind Block Auto-Defense, plus 3 Super Psionic powers of choice (not Psi-Sword/Psi-Shield); I.S.P. 3D6x10+10 per level.', '3-4 ft wingspan; body 1-2 ft long; tail 3-4 ft', 'Less than 20 lbs', '80-125 years', 'Northern Hinterlands and Northern Wilderness/Eastern Territory of the Palladium World', 'Humans and Elves (drawn to their company); sometimes noble knights, warriors, kings, clergy', 'Mostly evildoers; savage races such as Coyles, Orcs, Goblins', NULL, 'A bat-bird-cat hybrid psychic native to the Palladium World that reads a person''s true name to reveal their past and foretell their future.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.182-184');
  'wing-tips', 'Wing Tips', 'faerie', 'rifts', 0, 'Any, but mostly Principled (40%), Scrupulous (30%) or Unprincipled (20%)', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"4D6","MA":"5D6","PS":"1D6","PP":"5D6","PE":"2D6","PB":"5D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '3D6+2', '1D4x10', 'ME+100', 'Spd is 4D6 hopping around or 1D6x10+70 flying. A.R. is stated as not applicable.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+10, S.D.C. 1D6+2', NULL, 9, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"dodge":4}', '+1 initiative, +4 automatic dodge (does not use an attack), +3 all saving throws; magic aura grants nearby creatures within 30 ft +3 vs magic (not psionics) and +20% vs coma/death.; attacks per melee: 4 (psionics only); dodge: +4 automatic', 'Communicate via Telepathy; Land Navigation 98%, Wilderness Survival 80%, Identify Plants and Fruit 80%, Sing by whistling 90%.', 'Flight and magic aura; no visible eyes, ears, nose, or mouth yet has exceptional sight and hearing; communicates only by Telepathy or Empathy; chirps and whistles somehow.', 'None (radiates a passive magic aura; see bonuses)', 'I.S.P. M.E.+100; proficiency equal to 6th-level Mind Mage/Mind Melter. 1st ed. Palladium Fantasy characters get psi-powers levels 1-4. Rifts/2nd ed. characters get all Healing, Sensitive and Physical powers plus Bio-Manipulation, Empathic Transmission, Hypnotic Suggestion, Mind Block Auto-Defense, Group Mind Block, Mind Bolt, and Bio-Regeneration (M.D.C.).', '2 ft wingspan; body the size of an orange or softball', '2-4 lbs', 'Unknown; some believe them immortal, though easily destroyed', 'Forests of the Eastern Territory and Great Northern Wilderness of the Palladium World; rumored in the Magic Zone (Ohio valley) on Earth', 'None per se, but known to associate with humans, Elves, Drakin, and creatures of good alignment', 'Forest predators; unscrupulous humanoids', NULL, 'A tiny, eyeless flying creature resembling feathered wings on a fuzzy ball that uses psionics to comfort others and rarely fights.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.184');
  'taut-blow-worms', 'Taut: Blow Worms', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered Anarchist; attacks only to feed or when provoked', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6+30","PP":"1D6+10","PE":"2D6+18","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D4x100', '2D4', NULL, 'P.S. is Supernatural on Rifts Earth. The 10-foot inner epidermis (its vulnerable interior) has 6D6 M.D.C.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 3D4x10, S.D.C. 3D4x10, A.R. 7', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1}', '+1 strike with body, +3 strike with glob, +5 save vs poison/toxins, +2 save vs magic/psionic attacks.; attacks per melee: 3 (1 glob spit + 2 crush/smash); strike: +1 body, +3 glob', NULL, 'Virtually blind but tracks by smell (89%) and motion-sensing receptors (700 ft range); burrows at speed 8, swims 19%; spits a huge immobilizing mucus glob before swallowing prey whole.', NULL, NULL, '120-200 ft long', '1D4 tons', '600 years', 'Infrequent worldwide as a result of summoning; needs a cool, dark, damp burrowing environment; dies in 1D4 days in hot sun', 'None; tolerates fellow Worms of Taut', 'None', NULL, 'A massive, blind demon-worm that immobilizes prey by spitting sticky mucus globs, then swallows victims whole.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.185-186');
  'taut-fire-worms', 'Taut: Fire Worms', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered Diabolic evil', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D4","PS":"2D6+6","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+6","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6+10"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6+40', '2D6', NULL, 'I.Q. formula is qualified as animal intelligence. Hit Points/S.D.C./A.R. figures given apply on S.D.C. worlds.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 2D6+40, S.D.C. 2D6+12, A.R. 6', NULL, 13, '{"attacks":3,"strike":1,"dodge":1}', '+1 strike by bite, +2 strike with fire ball, +1 dodge, +2 all saves; impervious to fire/heat; vulnerable to cold (double damage).; attacks per melee: 3, usually by fire bolts; strike: +1 bite, +2 fireball', NULL, 'Climbs 40%, swims 30%, tracks by smell 66%, prowls 60%; infrared vision/heat sensor grants +1 to strike; burrows at speed 6; impervious to fire, vulnerable to cold.', NULL, NULL, '3 ft long', '15 lbs', '260 years', 'Infrequent worldwide via summoning; prefers hot/dry climates and the Yin-Sloth Jungles; dies quickly in cold', 'None; tolerated by other Worms of Taut', 'None', NULL, 'A small, aggressive fire-spitting demon-worm that thrives in hot, dry terrain and dies quickly in cold.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.186-187');
  'taut-nippers', 'Taut: Nippers', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered diabolic; extremely hostile, aggressive night predator', '{"IQ":"1D4+3","ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+10","PP":"2D6+6","PE":"2D6+10","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D4x10+10', '2D6', NULL, 'Hit Points/S.D.C./A.R. figures given apply on S.D.C. worlds.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 2D6+40, S.D.C. 2D6+20, A.R. 10', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":2,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":3}', '+2 initiative, +2 strike, +3 parry/dodge, +2 save vs all magic.', 'Can be taught basic commands in any language and a degree of obedience to a master, like a dog.', 'Nightvision 120 ft, climbs 90% (poor digger, shallow burrows only), prowls 56%, swims 40%, leaps 6 ft; articulated tail whips, constricts, or entangles.', NULL, NULL, '10-12 ft long (60% tail)', '60-75 lbs', '240 years', 'Infrequent worldwide via summoning; flourish in Central/South American jungles; still uncommon overall', 'None; tolerates fellow Worms of Taut', 'Humanoids and mammals', NULL, 'A fast, multi-legged salamander-like demon that hunts in packs and constricts prey with its snake-like tail.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.187');
  'taut-serpent-beasts', 'Taut: Serpent Beasts', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Miscreant or Diabolic', '{"IQ":"1D4+5","ME":"1D6+6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+16","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+16","PB":"1D6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10+40', '3D6', NULL, 'I.Q. is described as near-human. Hit Points/S.D.C./A.R. figures given apply on S.D.C. worlds.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 1D4+40, S.D.C. 1D4x10+40, A.R. 10', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":6,"initiative":4,"strike":4,"parry":4,"dodge":4}', '+4 initiative, +4 strike/parry/dodge, +2 save vs magic, impervious to poison, +10 save vs Horror Factor.', 'Speaks no language but learns basic commands and understands rudimentary words/conversation (about 40%); some can be taught a handful of guttural words.', 'Nightvision 90 ft, superhuman hearing and smell (detects new scent within 300 ft even while asleep), tracks by smell 85%, swims 70%, climbs 40%; impervious to poisons/chemicals; only half penalties if blinded.', NULL, NULL, '25-30 ft long', '900-1200 lbs', '1200 years', 'Uncommon worldwide via summoning; adapts to any climate except cold', 'None; tolerates fellow Worms of Taut and works with other supernatural fiends or powerful sorcerers', 'All humanoids (seen as prey)', NULL, 'A grisly serpent with four stubby legs and a human-like head that hibernates between kills and poisons victims with its bite.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.187-188');
  'taut-tri-fang', 'Taut: Tri-Fang', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered Miscreant; very hostile, an aggressive predator', '{"IQ":"1D4","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"2D6+12","PP":"1D6+16","PE":"2D6+14","PB":"2D6","Spd":"3D6+6"}', NULL, NULL, '1D6x10+40', '3D6', NULL, 'I.Q. is described as low animal intelligence. Hit Points/S.D.C./A.R. figures given apply on S.D.C. worlds.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 3D6+30, S.D.C. 2D6+20, A.R. 9', NULL, 15, '{"attacks":7,"strike":3,"initiative":3,"dodge":6}', '+3 strike/initiative, +6 automatic dodge (acts like a parry due to speed).; attacks per melee: 7 (6 plus 1 acid spit); dodge: +6 automatic', NULL, 'Spits acid; nightvision 30 ft; swims 50%, climbs 60% (loves big trees), prowls 32%.', NULL, NULL, '16-20 ft', '500-600 lbs', '220 years', 'Infrequent worldwide via summoning; survives any climate except cold', 'None; tolerates fellow Worms of Taut', 'Men and most mammals', NULL, 'A three-headed serpent whose center head spits blinding acid at foes'' eyes while its coils constrict prey.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.188-189');
  'taut-tomb-worms', 'Taut: Tomb Worms', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Considered Diabolic', '{"ME":"1D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"1D6","PP":"1D6","PE":"2D6+12","PB":"1D6","Spd":"2D6"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6', '1D6', NULL, 'Horror Factor is 11 if only one or two are present, or 14 for five or more.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 3D6, S.D.C. 14, A.R. 8', NULL, NULL, '{"attacks":4,"strike":1,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+1 strike, +2 parry/dodge, +2 all saves, impervious to cold and disease; Horror Factor is 11 (one or two) or 14 (five or more) - see pools_note.', NULL, 'Nightvision 120 ft, climbs 50%, prowls 40%, swims 50%; smells blood/sickness/decay at 90% (1000 ft range), tracks scent 80%; burrows at speed 8; carrion eater, impervious to cold.', NULL, NULL, '2-2.5 ft long', '10-15 lbs', '600 years', 'Burial places and ruins worldwide', NULL, 'All life', NULL, 'A small scavenging demon-worm with razor teeth that swarms crypts and graveyards, boldly attacking the sick or helpless.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.189-190');
  'yema', 'Yema', 'undead', 'rifts', 0, 'None (zombie), but generally a tool for evil', '{"IQ":"2D6","ME":"3D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6+12","PP":"4D6","PE":"3D6+10","PB":"1D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '2D6x10+40', '2D4x10', NULL, 'Spd is 4D6 running or 1D6x10+40 flying.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points 2D4x10, S.D.C. 1D6x10+10, A.R. 14', NULL, 16, '{"attacks":4,"strike":3,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+3 strike, +2 parry/dodge, +4 all saves; impervious to all but magic and silver weapons; will not parry or dodge unless specifically ordered to.', 'Magically understands all spoken tongues.', 'Flight, keen hawk-like vision, bio-regenerates 2D6 M.D.C./melee; impervious to poison, drugs, magic toxins, psionics, and normal/Mega-Damage weapons; only magic and silver harm it (silver S.D.C. weapons deal equivalent M.D.).', 'All Level One and Two Air and Fire Warlock spells at 4th level proficiency', NULL, 'Wingspan 20-30 ft', '200-250 lbs', '400 years on Rifts Earth (only 4 years on the Palladium World)', 'Buried in ancient ruins in Ophid''s Grasslands and along nearby mountains/coast on the Palladium World; few Rifted to Earth', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'An undead, mindlessly obedient flying reptile reanimated as a spellcasting guardian or steed for its controlling master.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.190');
  'za', 'Za', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic (50%) or Miscreant (50%) only', '{"IQ":"2D6+1","ME":"2D6","MA":"1D6","PS":"4D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"4D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, 'PE+100', '3D4x10', NULL, 'Spd is 4D6 running or 2D4x10+50 flying. Hit Points/S.D.C./A.R. figures given apply on S.D.C. worlds.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+100, S.D.C. 1D6x10, A.R. 10', NULL, 14, '{"attacks":5,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":2}', '+1 initiative, +2 strike/parry/dodge, +4 dodge while flying, +1 pull punch, +2 roll with impact, +3 all saves; impervious to fire/heat.; attacks per melee: 5 physical or 2 elemental magic spells; dodge: +2 (+4 flying)', 'Magically understands and speaks all languages (totally illiterate); Basic Math 80%, Land Navigation 80%, Wilderness Survival 60%, Pick Pockets 50%, Pick Locks 50%, Palming 50%, Streetwise 60%; selects three ancient W.P.s and two energy W.P.s.', 'Flight, nightvision 60 ft, sees invisible, tracks by smell 76%, prowls 66%, bio-regenerates 2D4 M.D./melee; impervious to fire (even magic fire); stubby articulated fingers with an opposable thumb use tools/weapons.', 'Fire Elemental Magic: Stench of Hades, Cloud of Ash, Darkness, Fiery Touch, Circle of Flame, Wall of Flame, Fuel Flame, Fire Ball, Extinguish Fires; equal to a 4th-level Warlock, casts 8 spells daily, 2 spell attacks/melee in place of physical attacks', NULL, '4-5 ft long', '120-160 lbs', '2000 years', 'Gorges, grottos, caves, ruins, and dark rocky places; native to the Palladium World, not known to exist on Rifts Earth', 'None per se; may join forces with others for a vast treasure or magic items', 'Humans and humanoids; indifferent toward most others', NULL, 'A cruel, winged dog-like magic-user that hoards vast treasures in guarded lairs and hunts down thieves who steal from it.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.190-191');
  'zavor', 'Zavor', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Diabolic evil', '{"IQ":"1D6+1","ME":"2D6","MA":"2D6","PS":"3D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"2D6","Spd":"2D6"}', 'PE+20', '2D4x10', NULL, '3D6', NULL, 'No M.D.C. line is printed; the Zavor is an S.D.C.-frame creature whose bite/claw attacks nonetheless deal Mega-Damage. Natural S.D.C. Armor Rating is 8.', 8, 16, '{"attacks":3,"strike":2,"parry":3,"dodge":3}', '+2 strike, +3 parry/dodge; invulnerable to poison, drugs, fire, cold, fall damage, magic, and most Mega-Damage weapons; splits into a duplicate whenever struck by a qualifying magic attack or a magical creature''s physical attack.', 'Speaks Gobblely/Goblin 90%, Land Navigation 50%, W.P. Blunt.', 'Nightvision 90 ft, sees invisible, prowls 50%, climbs 60%; splits into an identical duplicate whenever struck by magic weapons/spells or a magical creature''s physical attack; only wood, silver, iron, and psionics can harm it.', 'No abilities other than being impervious to all magic', NULL, '3.5 ft tall', '45-70 lbs', 'Immortal - lives until slain', 'Secluded, desolate ruins and tunnels; known among the Baalgor Wastelands on the Palladium World; none known on Rifts Earth', 'Absolutely none', 'ALL life forms', NULL, 'A shy humanoid that becomes a relentless killer and multiplies into duplicates whenever struck by magic or a magical creature.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.191-192');
  'waternix', 'Waternix', 'monster', 'rifts', 0, 'Any (mostly Anarchist 50%; also evil; rarely Unprincipled 5%)', '{"IQ":"3D6","ME":"4D6","MA":"3D6","PS":"2D6","PP":"3D6","PE":"3D6","PB":"4D6","Spd":"4D6"}', NULL, NULL, '4D6x10', '4D6', NULL, 'Spd 4D6 running (x3 for flight). SDC (3D6), HP (PE+20) and AR (9) apply only in non-MDC (S.D.C.) settings; on Rifts Earth it is a Mega-Damage creature (M.D.C. 4D6x10) with no separate hit points.; In S.D.C. settings: hit points PE+20, S.D.C. 3D6, A.R. 9', NULL, 12, '{"attacks":4,"initiative":1,"strike":2,"parry":2,"dodge":4}', '+6 to dodge while in flight; +2 to all saving throws; AR 9 applies only in S.D.C. settings.', 'Hunting, Fishing +20%, Play 1D4 Musical Instruments, Dancing +5%, Basic Electronics +5%, Wilderness Survival +15%, Demon and Monster Lore +5%, Faerie Lore +10%, Basic Math +20%, Speaks Faerie Folk 98%, literate in 3 additional languages +20%, speaks 1D4 more languages +10%. Favors knives and light chain weapons, or modern handguns (esp. light lasers); cannot handle much larger/heavier weapons.', 'Flight, strong prowl/swim/climb, tracks by smell, nightvision, at-will invisibility, sees invisible, bio-regenerates 1D8 M.D./melee, powerful leaps (tripled in flight), dexterous tool-using paws; solitary, never runs in packs or with a mate.', 'None, unless a magic O.C.C., which is unlikely; may use magic items and potions', NULL, 'About fox/medium-dog sized: ~3 ft (0.9 m) long head to buttock; 4 to 4.5 ft (1.2-1.35 m) tall standing on hind legs, its usual posture', '20-45 lbs (9-20 kg)', '1000 years', 'Forests worldwide; uncommon in the deep south and jungles', 'None per se; friendly with Trolls; friendly with most Faerie Folk, especially cruel/wicked ones like Bogies, Pucks, Dead Moon Hags and Toad Stools', 'Powerful supernatural beings and clergy; dislikes all humanoids, especially humans and Elves', 'No full O.C.C.; only skill leanings: Thief (all Rogue skills plus Computer Operation, Computer Programming, Pilot Hover Vehicle, Locksmith; +12%), Ranger/Scout (all Wilderness skills plus Astronomy, Holistic Medicine, Intelligence, Detect Ambush, Cooking; +10%), Trickster (all Communications skills plus Escape Artist, Forgery, Palming, Concealment, Pilot Hover Vehicles, Read Sensory Equipment, Basic Mechanics; +10%), or Real Magic (learns only the magic and O.C.C. skills of a Ley Line Walker, Shifter, Wizard, Warlock, Witch, Diabolist or Summoner, no skill bonus; about 10% become mages, mostly Diabolists using Palladium Ward magic). Not recommended as a player character, but possible at G.M. discretion. NPC experience 1D4+2 level; PC 1D4 level, using the Dragon experience table at double cost per level, rarely reaching 8th level or higher.', 'A small winged, dog- or fox-like faerie creature that tricks and steals from humanoids for sport, rarely killing outright unless evil-aligned.', 'Rifts Conversion Book One p.181-182');





-- Read the result back. This script asserts its OWN rows and nothing else.
SELECT 'all 77 creatures are in' AS assertion, count(*) AS got, 77 AS want
